{"raw": {"https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Hospitality---Lecturer-Senior-Lecturer--Continuing-Educatn---Training-_JR-10000044130": {"title": "School of Hospitality - Lecturer/Snr Lecturer (Continuing Education & Training)", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-02\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] School of Hospitality - Lecturer/Senior Lecturer (Continuing Education & Training) [What you will be working on] \u2022 Deliver planned curriculum to adult learners in continuing education training (CET) programmes on scheduled weekdays, weeknights or occasional weekends. \u2022 Perform curriculum development, lesson design, course delivery and module(s) supervision roles in at least two of the following subject areas: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0AI Literacy, Digital transformation, and emerging technologies \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Hospitality Innovation, Technology and Sustainability \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Revenue Optimization and Management \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Service Quality and Customer Experience \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Culinary Arts and Entrepreneurship \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Wellness, Therapy and Spa Operations and Management \u00a0\u2022 Facilitate students\u2019 learning, perform assessment grading, and other academic duties such as invigilation. \u2022 Deliver and update of training materials, including manuals, guides and instructional videos. \u2022 Maintain accurate training records and provide regular reports to management on training outcomes and areas of improvement. [What we are looking for] \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0At least 8-10 years of relevant industry experience in hospitality, education, marketing, business development and/or consultancy. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0High-level written and verbal communication skills. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Experience supporting and working with cross-functional teams in a dynamic environment. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Strong industry links and exposures in related industry and sectors. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Experience in developing a curriculum or providing training in a client-facing environment. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Experience in designing or delivering training related to AI, digital transformation, automation, data analytics, or emerging technologies would be advantageous. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Applicants with WSQ Advanced Certificate in Learning and Performance (ACLP) and the WSQ Diploma in Design and Development of Learning for Performance (DDDLP) accreditation would be an advantage."}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/Office-of-Finance---Executive--2-year-contract-_JR-10000051618": {"title": "Office of Finance - Executive", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] Office of Finance - Executive [What you will be working on] 1. Involve in the financial aspects of Continuing Education Training (CET) programs, including billing, collections, processing financial schemes, and handling operational tasks. 2. Assist in managing the end-to-end grant claim process, including submission, tracking, reconciliation, and disbursement monitoring. 3. Follow up on pending, outstanding, or rejected claims with relevant stakeholders. 4. Undertake ad hoc projects as assigned. [What we are looking for] 1. Relevant qualification in accounting, business or finance. Public Sector finance experience will be an advantage.\u00a0 2. Proficient in MS Word, Excel and PowerPoint. 3. Good writing and verbal communication skills. 4. Effective team player, meticulous, analytical, systematic, and resourceful."}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/Office-of-the-Registrar---Assistant-Manager--Admissions-Systems-_JR-10000050432": {"title": "Office of the Registrar - Assistant Manager (Admissions Systems)", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] Office of the Registrar - Assistant Manager (Admissions Systems) [What you will be working on] We are looking for a meticulous and motivated individual to manage and oversee the end-to-end enhancement, testing and rollout of admissions systems supporting Polytechnics and ITE. The role serves as the key liaison between MOE, participating Institutes of Higher Learning (IHLs) and the appointed system vendor to ensure that system enhancements are delivered according to agreed requirements, timelines and quality standards, and are aligned with admissions policies and processes. This position will be on a 2-year contract. Job Description \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Manage and oversee the end-to-end lifecycle of the system enhancement projects, from requirements gathering through development, testing, rollout and post go live support.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Keep track of project plans, timelines, issue logs and risk registers to track progress and ensure timely delivery.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Monitor vendor deliverables against agreed scope, specifications, milestones and service levels.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Escalate project risks, issues and dependencies appropriately, and recommend mitigation actions. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Work closely with MOE and IHLs to gather, analyse and document business and functional requirements.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Translate admissions policies and operational workflows and considerations into clear system requirements. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Manage User Acceptance Testing (UAT) and coordinate defect logging, triage and resolution with the vendor. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Support production setup, cutover planning and system rollout activities. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Monitor system performance post\u2011deployment and follow through on the rectification of bugs, issues or gaps identified after go\u2011live. [What we are looking for] \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Relevant qualification with at least 3 years of relevant work in IHL admissions, IT system projects, system enhancements or project coordination. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Familiarity with admissions processes, Full Subject-Based Banding, student systems or the education sector would be advantageous \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Strong coordination, documentation and stakeholder management skills. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Able to work effectively with multiple agencies and vendors, with good follow\u2011through and attention to detail. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0High level of accuracy in data handling and reporting"}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/Office-of-the-Registrar---Deputy-Manager--Student-Records-and-Graduation-_JR-10000053782": {"title": "Office of the Registrar - Deputy Manager (Student Records and Graduation)", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] We are looking for a meticulous and motivated individual to manage student records (which include student\u2019s status and particulars, and academic records such as diploma certificates and academic transcripts), and processes and systems relating to student data including deferment, withdrawal and dismissal. Additionally, this role will also be one of the key team members in planning, organising and executing the RP\u2019s graduation ceremony. [What you will be working on] \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Manage processes relating to changes to non-academic and academic student records by ensuring that the processes are user-centric, adhere to guidelines and policies, and optimised via process improvements and use of suitable digitalisation tools. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Ensure relevant processes are properly documented and kept up-to-date. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Plan, organise and execute tasks (including procurement, event management and relevant processes, such as registration of graduands, seats and tickets management, on-stage proceedings and display of graduands\u2019 name on screen) for RP\u2019s graduation ceremony. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Ensure that relevant systems are working according to business requirements, and provide business requirements for new systems or system enhancements and perform User Acceptance Tests (UATs) when required.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Prepare data accurately for internal and external reporting in timely manner. [What we are looking for] \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Self-motivated, highly resourceful, and committed individual, capable of working both independently and as part of a team. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Relevant experience in similar process-focused roles and system-related work, preferably in the education sector.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0High level of accuracy in data handling and reporting\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Strong critical thinking, analytical, planning, and organisational skills. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Proficient in Microsoft Office, Microsoft 365 and digital/automation tools (e.g. SharePoint, Power Automate, RPA)"}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/Office-of-the-Registrar---Manager--Admissions-_JR-10000049140": {"title": "Office of the Registrar - Manager (Admissions)", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] We are looking for a meticulous and motivated individual to lead a team of officers in managing full-time diploma admissions, data requests and analysis. The candidate should have good understanding of the tertiary education landscape and be able to recommend strategies for intake planning. Those with vast prior experience and a good track record in managing tertiary admissions or similar operational roles may be considered for a more senior position with a larger job size. [What you will be working on] \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Plan and administer admission exercises, including end-to-end admissions process from application review to offer and enrolment \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Process applications in alignment with institutional policies and admission criteria.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Review existing processes and propose enhancements to manage the admission exercises in a timely and accurate manner \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Monitor, analyse and report trends in admissions and course demand \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Manage course streaming and course transfer processes \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Maintain a strong understanding of the admissions policies and procedures, and work with internal stakeholders and external agencies on implementation of admission processes \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Manage systems enhancement and development, including requirement gathering, user acceptance test and data verification \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Review, plan and deliver customer-centric services and procedures \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Manage admissions related enquiries and appeals [What we are looking for] \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Relevant qualification with at least 5 years of relevant work experience with at least 3 years of experience in leading a team \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Prior work experience from another educational institution would be advantageous \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0High level of accuracy in data handling and reporting \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Able to multi-task and handle competing priorities within tight timeline \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Strong analytical skills with the ability to work independently as well as in a team \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Excellent communication skills (both spoken and written) and interpersonal skills \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0IT savvy and proficient in using Microsoft Office applications \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Knowledge in the use of tools for accurate and efficient analysis of large quantity of data such as Excel VBA, Python or R programming would be advantageous"}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Applied-Science---Lecturer-Senior-Lecturer--Biomedical-Science-_JR-10000054819": {"title": "School of Applied Science - Lecturer/Senior Lecturer (Biomedical Science)", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] School of Applied Science - Lecturer/Senior Lecturer (Biomedical Science) [What you will be working on] Lecturer will undertake curriculum development and delivery of diploma-related modules as well as be involved in applied science-based research projects. Candidates should possess relevant work or research experience in the Life Science/Biomedical Science Industry.\u00a0 Job Responsibilities: \u2022 Teach relevant subjects in pre-employment and continuing education training programmes \u2022 Design and develop course materials for pre-employment and continuing education training programmes \u2022 Lead or participate in consultancy and research projects \u2022 Supervise students for projects \u2022 Mentor and assist in tracking students\u2019 academic and non-academic performance \u2022 Partake in administrative duties related to the diploma course or within the school \u2022 Deliver planned curriculum for continuing education training programmes on scheduled weekday evenings or weekends and participate in assessment activities [What we are looking for] \u2022 Relevant qualification in the field of Life Science/Biomedical Science-related disciplines. \u2022 Candidates should possess at least five years of relevant work experience in areas related to Molecular and Cellular Biology, Genetics, Biomedical Informatics, Bioinformatics, Health Informatics and/or Omics.\u00a0 \u2022 Relevant experience with Generative AI, Data Analytics and Sustainability will be advantageous. \u2022 Candidates should have strong industry links and exposure, with experience in related sectors. \u2022 Candidates should be interested in strengthening the institute's professional network in the Biomedical Science sector \u2022 Strong communication and interpersonal skills with ability to build strong working relationships with people at all levels. \u2022 Proficient in IT, planning and organising skills."}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Business---Assoc-Lecturer--Digital-Business-and-Banking-and-Finance-_JR-10000054349": {"title": "School of Business - Assoc Lecturer (Digital Business and Banking and Finance)", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\nPart time\n\n[What the role is] As an Adjunct Lecturer, you will bring current industry knowledge into the classroom and help young and adult learners develop practical, workplace-relevant skills. Depending on the modules assigned, you will deliver lessons, facilitate applied learning and assess students in one of the specialisations below. [What you will be working on] Key Responsibilities \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Deliver scheduled lessons and facilitate learning for Pre-Employment Training (PET) and/or Continuing Education and Training (CET) students. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Prepare for classes using the approved curriculum and learning resources, and adapt delivery to support learners with different needs. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Facilitate hands-on activities, case discussions and problem-based learning using relevant industry examples and tools. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Assess students' work, provide timely feedback and complete grading and related academic administration within stipulated timelines. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Provide consultation and learning support to students for the assigned module. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Contribute industry insights to the review of lesson materials, assessments or applied projects where required. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Comply with RP's academic, assessment and administrative requirements. Areas of Specialisation Candidates should be able to teach in at least one of the following areas: 1. Digital Solutions and Business Technology \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Digital Business, AI, Automation, Data Visualisation, Business Technologies and Project Deployment. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Application of AI tools, workflow automation, CRM, analytics, e-commerce and low-code/no-code platforms to business problems. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Business needs analysis, solution design, prototyping, testing and basic technical troubleshooting. 2. Banking and Finance \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Financial Technology, Analytics, Financial Markets, Corporate Finance, Investment Analysis, Trade Finance, Compliance, Risk Management and Sustainable Finance. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Application of real-world case studies, simulations and tools such as Excel, data analytics and AI applications. [What we are looking for] General Requirements \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Relevant academic qualifications in Business, Banking, Finance, Economics, Data Analytics, Business Technology or a related field. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0At least three years of relevant industry experience. Prior teaching, training or facilitation experience is advantageous. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Current industry knowledge and the ability to translate professional experience into practical learning. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0A nurturing mindset and the ability to establish a strong rapport with learners. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Strong communication and facilitation skills, with the ability to explain concepts clearly. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Reliable, organised and able to meet teaching, assessment and administrative timelines. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Comfortable using relevant digital and educational technologies for lesson delivery. 1. Digital Solutions and Business Technology \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Relevant experience in digital transformation, technology implementation, business analysis, product or project management, automation, CRM, e-commerce, marketing technology or data analytics. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Hands-on experience in deploying digital, automation or AI-enabled solutions, including workflows, prototypes or proof-of-concept solutions. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Able to analyse business problems, explain solution logic and troubleshoot basic issues involving workflows, configurations, data, integrations and outputs. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Shortlisted candidates may be asked to showcase a prior AI workflow or solution and present a short demonstration and teaching deck for a proposed one-hour lesson, including their lesson-design thought process. 2. Banking and Finance \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Strong expertise in one or more areas: banking operations; risk, compliance and AML/KYC; financial markets, treasury or investment products; fintech, digital banking or data analytics; sustainable finance or ESG. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Good understanding of trends shaping the financial sector, including digitalisation, AI, regulation and sustainability. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Relevant professional certifications such as CFA, FRM, IBF or sustainability-related credentials are advantageous."}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Business---CET-Associate-Lecturer--Business-_JR-10000054827": {"title": "School of Business - CET Associate Lecturer (Business)", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\nPart time\n\n[What the role is] School of Business - CET Associate Lecturer (Business) [What you will be working on] Your responsibilities will include, but are not limited to, the following: \u2022 Teach relevant subjects in Continuing Education Training (CET) programmes \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Design and develop course materials for Continuing Education Training (CET) programmes in Business, Management, Marketing, Human Resources, Accounting, Finance, Sustainability, Digital Business, Artificial Intelligence, Entrepreneurship, or other related disciplines. \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Deliver planned curriculum to adult learners on scheduled weekday evenings or on weekends and participate in assessment activities \u2022 \u00a0 \u00a0Take up the role of Programme Coordinator for CET module when required [What we are looking for] \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Relevant qualifications in Business, Management, Marketing, Human Resources, Accounting, Finance, Sustainability, Digital Business, Artificial Intelligence, Entrepreneurship, or other related disciplines.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0At least five years of relevant industry experience in one or more business domains, such as marketing, digital transformation, human resources, finance, accounting, business operations, sustainability, entrepreneurship, or organisational development.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Training and Adult Education (TAE) Workforce Skills Qualification (WSQ) certifications such as Advanced Certificate in Learning and Performance (ACLP), Advanced Certificate in Training and Assessment (ACTA), or Diploma in Adult and Continuing Education (DACE) will be advantageous.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Passion for adult learning and the ability to facilitate learning for working professionals from diverse backgrounds.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Strong communication, presentation and interpersonal skills, with the ability to engage learners effectively and build strong working relationships with industry partners and stakeholders.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Sound planning, organisational and classroom facilitation skills, with a practical and learner-centric approach.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Proficient in the use of digital learning technologies, productivity tools and online collaboration platforms.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Prior experience in curriculum development, training delivery, coaching, mentoring, consultancy, or industry projects will be an added advantage."}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Singapore/School-of-Business---Lecturer--Business-_JR-10000042267": {"title": "School of Business - Lecturer (Business)", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] The job of a lecturer is immensely meaningful and significant. You will impart knowledge and skills, prepare young and adult learners for the working world, and nurture their development. The role also offers opportunities to develop contemporary curricula, conduct impactful lessons, participate in consultancy and applied research, and collaborate with industry partners. [What you will be working on] Core Responsibilities \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Deliver lessons, develop teaching and assessment materials, and facilitate learning for Pre-Employment Training (PET) and Continuing Education and Training (CET) students. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Enhance existing and/or develop new curricula and learning materials to strengthen students\u2019 application and employability. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Contribute to PET and CET modules and programmes, using appropriate GenAI and EdTech tools where applicable. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Participate in the development of teaching and learning capabilities within RP and the School\u2019s academic team. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Support the School\u2019s strategic initiatives through academic advancement, student development and industry projects. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Undertake academic administration, including setting assessments, grading submissions and coordinating academic reports. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Provide pastoral support and guide students through internships, final-year projects, competitions, career development and overseas learning activities. Areas of Specialisation Candidates are expected to contribute in at least one of the following specialisations: 1. Digital Solutions and Business Technology \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Design and deliver modules in Digital Business, AI, Automation, Data Visualisation, Business Technologies and Project Deployment. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Guide students in analysing business needs and designing practical technology-enabled solutions. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Conduct hands-on learning using AI tools, workflow automation, CRM, analytics, e-commerce and low-code/no-code platforms. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Support digital and AI consultancy projects from requirements gathering and solution design to testing and deployment. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Teach students to explore new and emerging technologies, troubleshoot basic technical issues and improve their solutions. 2. Banking and Finance \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Design and deliver modules in Financial Technology, Analytics and areas such as Financial Markets, Corporate Finance, Investment Analysis, Trade Finance, Compliance, Risk Management and Sustainable Finance. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Integrate real-world case studies, simulations and industry-relevant tools such as Excel, data analytics and AI applications into learning. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Collaborate with banks, fintech firms, regulators and professional bodies to co-develop curricula, projects and experiential learning opportunities. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Participate in consultancy, applied research and capability-building initiatives related to banking, finance and sustainability. [What we are looking for] General Requirements \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Relevant academic qualifications in Business, Banking, Finance, Economics, Data Analytics, Marketing, Business Technology or a related field. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0A nurturing mindset and the ability to establish a strong rapport with learners. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Strong industry connections that can bring real-world context and opportunities into the learning experience. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Ability to integrate relevant technology and current industry developments into teaching and learning. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0A collaborative, self-driven and resourceful team player who can manage multiple projects independently. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Strong communication, facilitation, project and stakeholder management skills. 1. Digital Solutions and Business Technology \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0At least three years of relevant experience in digital transformation, technology implementation, business analysis, product or project management, automation, CRM, e-commerce, marketing technology or data analytics. Teaching or training experience is an advantage. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Experience in managing or deploying digital, automation, technology or AI-enabled projects. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Ability to analyse business problems, identify root causes and translate needs into practical solution requirements. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Comfortable exploring new technologies and troubleshooting workflows, configurations, data, integrations and outputs. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Experience in developing and testing prototypes, proof-of-concept solutions, digital workflows or process improvements. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Able to explain technical concepts clearly to non-technical learners and stakeholders. 2. Banking and Finance \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0At least three years of relevant experience in banking, financial services, fintech or a related sector. Teaching or training experience is an advantage. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Strong expertise in one or more areas: banking operations; risk, compliance and AML/KYC; financial markets, treasury or investment products; fintech, digital banking or data analytics; sustainable finance or ESG. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Good understanding of trends shaping the financial sector, including digitalisation, AI, regulation and sustainability. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Experience with financial institutions, fintech firms, regulators or professional bodies is advantageous. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Relevant certifications such as CFA, FRM, IBF or sustainability-related credentials are a bonus."}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Engineering---Assistant-Manager-Deputy-Manager_JR-10000052471": {"title": "School of Engineering - Senior Executive/Assistant Manager", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] School of Engineering - Senior Executive/Assistant Manager [What you will be working on] To provide integrated administrative, procurement and student development support to ensure efficient school operations and enhance student engagement outcomes. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Provide guidance to academic staff on procurement and budgeting processes \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Perform end-to-end procurement (e.g. Small Value Purchases, Invitation To Quote, Request For Quote, Direct Contracting, Invitation To Tender) in accordance with government procurement guidelines \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Ensure compliance with organisational policies and support quality assurance audits with key stakeholders \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Maintain accurate data repositories and records to support reporting, compliance and decision-making \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Co-develop and implement student development programmes, leadership initiatives and engagement activities \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Support student club and activities to promote engagement and holistic development \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Support committees, meetings and school-wide events, including coordination, documentation and secretariat duties \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Leverage Microsoft 365 and digital/automation tools (e.g. SharePoint, Power Automate, RPA) to streamline workflows and enhance data management \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Undertake ad-hoc assignments and projects as required [What we are looking for] \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0At least 3 years of relevant experience, preferably in education administration \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Strong organisational, communication and coordination skills \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Team player with the ability to collaborate effectively across all levels \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Meticulous and self-driven, with strong attention to detail \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Able to work in a fast-paced environment and manage multiple priorities \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Proficient in Microsoft Office; familiar with Microsoft 365 and digital/automation tools (e.g. SharePoint, Power Automate, RPA) is preferred."}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Engineering---Associate-Lecturer--Aerospace-Engineering-_JR-10000035050": {"title": "School of Engineering - Associate Lecturer (Aerospace Engineering)", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\nPart time\n\n[What the role is] School of Engineering - Associate Lecturer (Aerospace Engineering) [What you will be working on] \u2022 Facilitate learners\u2019 learning, perform grading and assessment for Pre-employment Training (PET) and Continuing Education and Training (CET) based on Civil Aviation Authority of Singapore (CAAS) SAR-66 syllabus. \u2022 Development of CAAS SAR-66 curriculum for Pre-employment Training (PET) and Continuing Education and Training (CET). [What we are looking for] \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Qualification in Aerospace, Aeronautical or Mechanical Engineering or related discipline. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0At least 5 years of work experience in the aerospace MRO, with the following criteria(s): 1.\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0hold, or have held an aircraft maintenance license (B1 or B2 category) issued by CAAS, or 2.\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a05 years experience as an aircraft maintenance technician in the B1 Category and has passed CAAS SAR-66 basic examinations in the relevant B1 or B2 Category, or 3.\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Engineering degree in Aerospace, Aeronautical or Mechanical Engineering, and has passed CAAS SAR-66 basic examinations in in the relevant B1 or B2 Category. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Proficient in developing curriculum and delivering lessons related to CAAS SAR-66 curriculum in the relevant B1 or B2 Category \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Genuine passion to share knowledge and interact with youths, with strong communication and interpersonal skills. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Strong sense of initiative and the ability to work independently. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Excellent team player in collaborative settings."}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Engineering---Associate-Lecturer--Electrical---Electronic-Engineering-_JR-10000051372": {"title": "School of Engineering - Associate Lecturer (Electrical & Electronic Engineering)", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\nPart time\n\n[What the role is] Associate Lecturer (Electrical & Electronic Engineering) [What you will be working on] \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Adjunct teaching position, on an ad-hoc basis \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Deliver related courses in Electrical and Electronic Engineering, with stronger emphasis on Electrical and Power Engineering and Communications System domains \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Conduct engaging, hands-on training sessions on electrical installations, power systems, protection, testing & commissioning, and basic communication systems \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Facilitate adult learners\u2019 understanding of industry practices aligned to relevant standards and regulatory requirements (e.g., SS638, SS650) \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Guide learners through practical exercises, case studies, and real-world applications in electrical system design, operation, and maintenance \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Mentor and support learners in applying theoretical concepts to workplace scenarios, including troubleshooting and safety practices \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Collaborate with course teams to enhance curriculum delivery and ensure positive learning outcomes [What we are looking for] \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Qualification in Electrical Engineering, Power Engineering, Electronic and Communications Engineering, or a related discipline \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Strong industry experience in electrical installations, power systems, or facilities / energy management \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Familiarity with relevant Singapore standards and electrical regulatory frameworks is preferred \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Broad foundation in general electronics and electrical engineering, with deeper expertise in power engineering applications \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Prior experience in adult learning, training delivery, or industry mentoring is an advantage \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Ability to deliver hands-on, application-focused training for working professionals \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Strong passion for teaching, knowledge sharing, and developing industry-relevant competencies \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Excellent communication and interpersonal skills \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a team environment"}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Engineering---Lecturer--Aerospace-Engineering-_JR-10000043310": {"title": "School of Engineering - Lecturer (Aerospace Engineering)", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] Lecturer (Aerospace Engineering) [What you will be working on] \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Develop curriculum and deliver lessons, primarily in the areas of Singapore Airworthiness Requirement Part 66 (SAR-66) M1 to M17 modules, as well as other Engineering disciplines. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Supervise students\u2019 final year projects and internships, and reach out to various stakeholders such as industry partners and universities. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Develop and conduct Continuing Education and Training (CET) lessons. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Take part in academic research projects, R&D/Implementation projects or consultancy to the industry. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Mentor and motivate students in their learning journey. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Plan and lead in school activities such as student overseas trip, service learning, outreach events and similar activities. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Undertake other administrative work related to the programme and student development activities. [What we are looking for] \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Qualification in Aerospace, Aeronautical, Mechanical Engineering, Electrical/Electronic Engineering or related discipline. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0At least 5 years of work experience in the aerospace MRO, with the following criteria(s): 1.\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0hold, or have held an aircraft maintenance license (B1 and/or B2 category) issued by CAAS, or 2.\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a05 years experience as an aircraft maintenance technician in the B1 and/or B2 Category and has passed relevant CAAS SAR-66 basic examinations in, or 3.\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0engineering degree in Aerospace, Aeronautical, Mechanical, Electrical or Electronic Engineering, and has passed the relevant CAAS SAR-66 basic examinations for B1 and/or B2 Category. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Genuine passion to share knowledge and interact with youths, with strong communication and interpersonal skills. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Strong sense of initiative and the ability to work independently. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Excellent team player in collaborative settings. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Ability to perform in a fast-paced environment and in meeting deadlines. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Strong industry linkages in the related fields."}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Engineering---Lecturer--Aviation-Management-_JR-10000022677": {"title": "School of Engineering - Lecturer (Aviation Management)", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] Lecturer (Aviation Management) [What you will be working on] \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Deliver curriculum and assess student learning for youth and adult learners via face-to-face and e-learning modes. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Supervise students on projects and internships. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Mentor students and track their academic and non-academic performance.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Demonstrate the ability to learn and adopt EdTech tools, and stay abreast of technological advancements and emerging trends in the air transport sector. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Initiate and develop industry-linked collaborations and projects with industry partners. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Participate in academic or industry research to support curriculum and student development. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Conduct programme development activities such as mentoring, portfolio development, internship supervision, career guidance, competition training, certification coaching, school branding and outreach, and other administrative duties as assigned.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Deliver planned curriculum to adult learners on scheduled weekday evenings or on weekends and participate in assessment activities. [What we are looking for] \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Relevant qualifications in the air transport sector. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0At least three years of relevant industry experience preferably in ground handling and services or in flying commercial or military aircraft. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Well-versed in the domain areas of Airport Operations and Ground Handling. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Strong industry linkages in the related fields. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Passion for education and possess strong interest for mentoring, teaching and motivating both youth and adult learners. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Strong sense of initiative and the ability to work independently. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0A team player who thrives in collaborative environments. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Adaptable and able to work under tight timelines. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Excellent oral and written communication skills. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Strong interpersonal skills with the ability to build effective working relationships at all levels. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Sound planning and organising skills, practical and responsible."}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Engineering---Lecturer--Common-Engineering-Programme-_JR-10000009636": {"title": "School of Engineering - Lecturer (Common Engineering Programme)", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] School of Engineering - Lecturer (Common Engineering Programme) [What you will be working on] \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Develop curriculum and deliver lessons to full-time diploma (PET) students in areas of Mathematics, Statistics, Programming as well as other Engineering disciplines. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Develop and conduct Continuing Education and Training (CET) courses for adult learners. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Handle administrative work relating to teaching and managing modules which include crafting and marking assessments. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Lead or participate in academic research projects, data analysis projects, R&D/Implementation projects and/or poly-wide projects. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Enhance students\u2019 learning through activities such as supervising projects and internships, training students for competitions, and leading them on educational programmes, students' overseas trips or service-learning events. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Support students in providing pastoral care and guidance. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Involve in school activities such as outreach events and similar activities. [What we are looking for] \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0A qualification in Engineering or related discipline. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Preferably with at least 3 years of relevant industry experience in the Engineering field. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Strong interest in the development of curriculum especially for Mathematics, Statistics and/or Programming. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Technically competent, as well as have a passion and genuine interest to share knowledge and interact with youth and adults. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Have experience in Data Analytics (hands-on data manipulation, data modelling and data visualisation). \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Have experience in using Statistical Modelling tools such as R, Python, MATLAB or SPSS and Visual Analytics Technologies such as Tableau or Power BI. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Have strong communication and interpersonal skills with the ability to build strong working relationships with management and colleagues. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Possess sound planning, organising, writing and multi-tasking skills, with a strong sense of commitment and responsibility for completing assigned tasks on time. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Highly motivated, and able to work independently and in a team."}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Engineering---Lecturer--Electrical---Semiconductor-Engineering-_JR-10000053804": {"title": "School of Engineering - Lecturer (Electrical & Semiconductor Engineering)", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] School of Engineering - Lecturer (Electrical Engineering, Semiconductor Technology & Manufacturing) [What you will be working on] \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Deliver and develop lessons in electrical engineering, electronics, microelectronics and semiconductor technology.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Teach topics such as circuit analysis, analogue and digital electronics, semiconductor devices, IC fundamentals, instrumentation and engineering applications.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Deliver semiconductor modules covering wafer fabrication, process integration, semiconductor manufacturing, testing, packaging, reliability and yield engineering.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Develop curriculum, laboratories and projects involving AI-enabled semiconductor manufacturing, smart factories, semiconductor data analytics, intelligent process control, computer vision and Industry 4.0 technologies.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Develop and conduct CET programmes, including Specialist Diploma and Part-time Diploma courses.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Supervise student projects, internships and applied learning activities.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Collaborate with industry and university partners on curriculum development, applied projects and industry engagement.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Support outreach activities, student development and administrative duties. [What we are looking for] \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Strong fundamentals in electronics, electrical engineering, semiconductor devices and microelectronics.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Knowledge or exposure in one or more areas:\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Semiconductor manufacturing and wafer fabrication \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Equipment, process or product engineering \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Testing, reliability or yield engineering \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Advanced packaging or semiconductor automation \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Interest or experience in AI for semiconductor applications, including:\u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0- Yield prediction \u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0- Defect detection and classification \u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0- Computer vision for wafer inspection \u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0- Predictive maintenance \u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0- Manufacturing analytics \u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0- Digital twins \u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0- Smart manufacturing and Industry 4.0 \u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0- AI-enabled process optimisation \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Exposure to emerging technologies such as advanced packaging, chiplets, silicon photonics, AI accelerators, high-bandwidth memory (HBM) or SiC/GaN devices will be advantageous. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Ability to utilise AI tools for engineering, teaching and applied projects.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Passion for teaching, mentoring and engaging youths.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Strong communication and interpersonal skills."}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Engineering---Lecturer--Electrical-Eng---Next-Gen-Connectivity-_JR-10000053808": {"title": "School of Engineering - Lecturer (Electrical Eng & Next-Gen Connectivity)", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] School of Engineering - Lecturer (Electrical Engineering, Communications & Next-Generation Connectivity) [What you will be working on] \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Deliver and develop lessons in electrical engineering, electronics and communications engineering.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Teach topics such as circuit analysis, analogue and digital electronics, instrumentation, communication systems, RF fundamentals, antennas, optical fibre communications, wireless communications and communication networks.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Deliver emerging topics including 5G/5G-Advanced, 6G fundamentals, Open RAN, private 5G, IoT/AIoT, LPWAN, edge computing, cloud-native telecommunications and smart-city connectivity.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Develop laboratories and projects involving AI-enabled wireless communications, network optimisation, intelligent radio resource management, AI-assisted network planning, network analytics and AI-native communications systems.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Develop and conduct CET programmes, including Specialist Diploma and Part-time Diploma courses.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Supervise student projects, internships and applied learning activities.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Collaborate with industry and university partners on curriculum development, applied projects and industry engagement.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Support outreach activities, student development and administrative duties. [What we are looking for] \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Strong fundamentals in electronics, electrical engineering, communications and networking.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Knowledge or exposure in one or more areas:\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Wireless or mobile communications \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Communication networks and IP networking \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0RF systems or optical communications \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a05G/5G-Advanced, IoT or edge computing \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Interest or experience in AI/ML applications for communications, such as:\u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0- AI-enabled network optimisation \u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0- Network analytics \u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0- Intelligent wireless planning \u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0- Predictive network maintenance \u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0- AI-assisted communications systems \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Ability to utilise AI tools for engineering, teaching and applied projects.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Passion for teaching, mentoring and engaging youths.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Strong communication and interpersonal skills."}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Engineering---Lecturer--Electrical-Engineering-_JR-10000054856": {"title": "School of Engineering - Lecturer (Electrical Engineering)", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] School of Engineering - Lecturer (Electrical Engineering) [What you will be working on] \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Deliver and develop lessons in general electronics, electrical and power engineering, including electrical installations, power systems, protection, testing & commissioning. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Develop and conduct Continuing Education and Training (CET) for Specialist Diploma and Part-time Diploma. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Supervise students\u2019 final year projects and internships and reach out to various stakeholders such as industry partners and universities. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Take part in academic research projects, R&D/Implementation projects or consultancy to the industry. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Mentor and motivate students in their learning journey \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Involve in school activities such as service learning, outreach events, student overseas trips and similar activities. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Undertake other administrative work related to the programme and student development activities. [What we are looking for] \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Good fundamentals in Electrical and Electronic Engineering, or a related discipline, with strong fundamentals in electrical and power systems. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Knowledge or experience in electrical installations, power systems, or facilities / energy management \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Familiarity with power engineering, electrical systems, electrical safety practices, and regulations used in real-world electrical work. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Ability to apply readily available AI tools (including generative or agent-based AI) to support engineering work, teaching, or applied problem-solving in electrical, electronic, or communications domains. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Experience in applied projects, research, development work, or industry collaboration related to communications, electrical engineering, smart systems, or AI-enabled solutions is desirable. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Ability to guide students in projects, internships, or applied learning, and to mentor students in both technical and professional development. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Willingness to contribute to school activities, industry engagement, outreach programmes, and administrative duties related to programme and student development. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Genuine passion to share knowledge and interact with youths, with strong communication and interpersonal skills \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Ability to work independently and as a team player."}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Engineering---Lecturer--Mobility---Robotic-Systems-_JR-10000053810": {"title": "School of Engineering - Lecturer (Mobility & Robotic Systems)", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] School of Engineering - Lecturer (Mobility & Robotic Systems) [What you will be working on] \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Curriculum development, course delivery and student project supervision in the areas of large mobility and smart robotic engineering systems. This includes, but is not limited to, automation, manufacturing, advanced robotic systems such as Industry 4.0/5.0 and Intelligent Transport Systems, including Autonomous Vehicles (AVs) and Electric Vehicles (EVs).\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Develop and conduct Continuing Education and Training (CET) lessons. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Spearhead and identify new opportunities, initiatives and collaborations with industry. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Undertake project development or consultancy work with industry. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Perform other administrative work related to the programme. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Undertake student development activities. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Mentor and motivate students in their learning journey. [What we are looking for] \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Qualification in electrical / electronic / mechanical / mechatronic engineering or a related discipline, preferably with at least 1 year of experience in design, deployment, and commissioning of robotics, automation systems, or Intelligent Transport Systems. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Possess excellent initiative, strong multitasking skills, and a strong sense of responsibility for completing assigned duties on time. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Ability to work independently as well as collaboratively as an excellent team player. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Comfortable with programming and electronics, such as Arduino, Raspberry Pi, Python, or similar platforms, hands-on experiences in Robotics, Robot Operating System (ROS), Robot Programming, Industry 4.0/5.0, Industrial Internet of Things (IIoT), Collaborative/Mobile Robots or Intelligent Transport Systems will be an advantage."}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Engineering---Lecturer--Sustainable-Built-Environment-_JR-10000053811": {"title": "School of Engineering - Lecturer (Sustainable Built Environment)", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] School of Engineering - Lecturer (Sustainable Built Environment) [What you will be working on] \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Design and deliver lessons to full-time diploma students in areas such as Heating, Ventilation and Air Conditioning (HVAC), Air Conditioning and Mechanical Ventilation (ACMV), Building Services Engineering, energy management, Green Buildings, sustainability and related Built Environment disciplines. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Integrate industry-relevant technologies and practices such as smart building systems, building analytics, digitalisation and Artificial Intelligence (AI) applications into teaching and learning. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Develop and conduct Continuing Education and Training (CET) programmes for adult learners and industry professionals. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Design assessments and undertake curriculum development, course delivery and student learning responsibilities. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Supervise student internships, final-year projects and industry-based learning activities. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Mentor and guide students in their academic, professional and personal development. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Initiate, lead and manage Technology, Innovation and Enterprise (TIE) projects, including industry consultancy, commissioned projects, applied research and innovation initiatives. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Identify opportunities for industry-funded projects, grants and collaborations with companies, government agencies and professional bodies. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Build and maintain strong partnerships with stakeholders in the Built Environment sector to support education, innovation and industry engagement. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Participate in programme administration, outreach activities and other school-wide initiatives. [What we are looking for] \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Qualification in Mechanical Engineering, Building Services Engineering, Sustainable Built Environment, Facilities Management, Energy Engineering, Architecture, Engineering or a related discipline. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Preferably with at least 3 years of relevant industry experience in Heating, Ventilation and Air Conditioning (HVAC), Air Conditioning and Mechanical Ventilation (ACMV), Green Mark consultancy, Building Services Engineering, energy efficiency, sustainability, Facilities Management, or related Built Environment sectors. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Strong technical knowledge in ACMV/HVAC systems, energy-efficient building services, building energy performance, Green Mark requirements and sustainable building technologies. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Familiarity with smart building systems, building analytics, digitalisation, Artificial Intelligence (AI), Internet of Things (IoT), Building Information Modelling (BIM) or related technologies would be advantageous. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Experience in managing or participating in industry projects, consultancy assignments, commissioned projects, grant-funded projects or innovation initiatives would be advantageous. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Passionate about education and committed to nurturing both youth and adult learners. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Strong communication, presentation and stakeholder management skills. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Possess sound planning, organisational and project management skills, with a strong sense of responsibility and the ability to manage multiple priorities effectively. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Self-motivated and able to work independently as well as collaboratively in multidisciplinary teams."}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Engineering---Project-Staff--Robotics-and-Unmanned-Systems-_JR-10000053820": {"title": "School of Engineering - Project Staff (Robotics and Unmanned Systems)", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] We are seeking a versatile and forward-thinking Development Engineer/Specialist to join our team in advancing the boundaries of Physical and Embodied AI. In this role, you will bridge the gap between intelligent software and the physical world, transforming AI models into tangible, autonomous capabilities. You will design, prototype, and deploy AI-enabled physical systems\u2014such as robotics, unmanned platforms, and smart automation solutions\u2014utilizing ROS2.0. You will also act as a bridge between technology, industry partners, and academia, fostering ecosystem growth through knowledge sharing, mentoring student projects, and leading live innovation showcases. If you are passionate about applied research, hands-on hardware-software integration, and inspiring others, we want to hear from you. [What you will be working on] 1. Physical & Embodied AI Development \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0System Design & Prototyping: Design, develop, and prototype intelligent physical systems, robotics, and advanced automation platforms leveraging ROS2.0. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Hardware-Software Integration: Integration of advanced AI models, computer vision, and operational systems with sensors, actuators, edge devices, and embedded systems. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Applied Research & Piloting: Drive feasibility studies and pilot programs involving AI-enabled automation, unmanned systems (UAVs/AGVs), and smart monitoring solutions. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0End-to-End Project Support: Manage the full lifecycle of applied research and proof-of-concept initiatives, including data preparation, rigorous experimentation, performance evaluation, comprehensive documentation, and post-deployment technical support. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Prototype Commercialization: Assist in translating high-potential AI prototypes into scalable, deployable, or licensable industry solutions. 2. Knowledge Sharing & Ecosystem Enablement \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Educational Mentorship: Support curriculum development and actively mentor student capstone and research projects in robotics and applied AI domains. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Stakeholder Collaboration: Partner closely with internal researchers and external industry stakeholders on collaborative innovation initiatives. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Technology Advocacy: Lead and support engaging AI and robotics demonstrations for lab visits, innovation showcases, and executive partner engagements. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Use Case Curation: Synthesize and curate compelling physical AI use cases to engage, educate, and inspire both academic and industrial audiences. [What we are looking for] \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Qualification in Robotics Engineering, Computer Science, Electrical/Electronic Engineering, Mechatronics, or a closely related quantitative field. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Robotics Architecture: Proven hands-on experience developing with ROS2 (Robot Operating System). Familiarity with robotic arms and humanoid robots, robot kinematics, dynamics, and simulation tools (e.g., Gazebo, Isaac Sim) is highly valued. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0AI & Computer Vision Integration: Practical experience deploying Machine Learning/Deep Learning models (e.g., PyTorch, TensorFlow) and computer vision frameworks (e.g., OpenCV) onto physical platforms. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Embedded Software Engineering: Proficiency in C++ and Python, with strong software development best practices (Git, clean architecture, code reviews). \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Hardware & Edge Systems: Experience working with microcontrollers and single-board computers (e.g., NVIDIA Jetson, Raspberry Pi). Solid understanding of hardware communication protocols (I2C, SPI, UART, CAN bus) and sensor fusion (LiDAR, IMUs, cameras). Soft Skills & Core Attributes \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Collaborative Mindset: Exceptional interpersonal skills with a proven ability to collaborate effectively across diverse teams of engineers, researchers, students, and corporate partners. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Communication & Presentation: Confident and articulate presenter capable of breaking down complex technical concepts into accessible demonstrations for non-technical audiences. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Passion in Educational Mentorship: Guiding student learning journeys and contributing to educational frameworks. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Adaptability: A thriving curiosity for ambiguous, fast-paced R&D environments where troubleshooting physical hardware requires creative problem-solving."}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Engineering---Research-Staff--Aquaculture-Water-Treatment-_JR-10000054858-1": {"title": "School of Engineering - Research Staff (Aquaculture Water Treatment)", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] Republic Polytechnic's School of Engineering (SEG), in collaboration with the School of Science (SAS), invites applications for a full-time Research Staff on a 12-month contract to support the DGF-funded project, \"Smart Water Treatment in Recirculating Aquaculture Systems (RAS) for Land-based Fish Farms.\" This applied R&D project focuses on developing an innovative smart water treatment system to improve water quality, reduce ammonia, pathogens, turbidity, biofilm, and algae, and enhance the sustainability of land-based aquaculture. The project integrates two proprietary technologies: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0DuoBioSonic \u2013 Dual-frequency ultrasonic cavitation for controlling pathogens, algae, biofilm, and turbidity.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0AquAPEX \u2013 Multicellular graphite electrolysis for ammonia and nitrogen removal.\u00a0 The successful candidate will contribute to prototype development, laboratory research, system integration, water quality analysis, field validation at commercial fish farms, and technology commercialisation. [What you will be working on] Key Responsibilities: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Conduct applied research on smart water treatment technologies for recirculating aquaculture systems (RAS).\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Perform laboratory experiments, aquaculture field trials, water quality monitoring, microbiological testing, and data analysis.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Develop, integrate, and evaluate prototype systems, sensors, and instrumentation.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Collaborate with industry partners to support technology validation and deployment.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Supervise final-year project students and interns involved in the project.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Support intellectual property (IP) development, technology transfer, and commercialisation activities.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Prepare technical reports, journal publications, presentations, and research grant proposals.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Manage laboratory equipment & consumables, procurement, safety compliance, and research products. [What we are looking for] \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Qualification in Environmental Engineering/Science, Water Engineering, Aquaculture Science, Marine/Ocean Engineering/Science, Chemical Engineering, Biotechnology, Applied Chemistry, Mechanical Engineering, Mechatronics, Biomedical Science, Food Science, Systems Engineering, or a related field. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Interest in water treatment, aquaculture, water quality monitoring, microbiology, and applied research. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Knowledge of sensors, instrumentation, experimental design, data acquisition, and data analysis is an advantage. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Experience in laboratory testing, microbiological analysis, aquaculture, or water quality assessment is preferred. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Self-motivated, hands-on, and able to work independently and in multidisciplinary teams of researchers, engineers, scientists and students. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Good report/technical writing skills. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Entry-level candidates are encouraged to apply."}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Engineering---Research-Staff--Cold-Storage---Cryogenic-Systems-_JR-10000054861": {"title": "School of Engineering - Research Staff (Cold Storage & Cryogenic Systems)", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] Are you ready to build next-generation, sustainable cold chain logistics for life-saving biopharmaceuticals? Republic Polytechnic's School of Engineering (SEG), in strategic partnership with industry leader SSW Group, is seeking an ambitious full-time Research Staff (12-month contract) to engineer an industrial-scale 1\"m\" ^3 self-sustained passive cold storage platform under a DGF-funded initiative. Current biopharmaceutical distribution relies on massive active energy inputs and heavy daily coolant consumption. This project completely disrupts that model by building a zero-power-in-transit, high-performance thermal container (1\"m\"\u00d71\"m\"\u00d71\"m\" ) capable of locking in sub-zero temperatures (2\u20138\u00b0C) for over 72 continuous hours in harsh tropical environments. Beyond standard transport, this passive design provides critical fail-safe protection against warehouse power outages and opens up new pathways for long-haul air and sea freight to distant international markets without relying on active electrical refrigeration networks. You will lead the hands-on engineering across two breakthrough technological pillars: - Active-Passive \"Flash-Charging\" Cryogenic System: A rapid-charging base station interface utilizing specialized heat exchangers and Liquid Nitrogen (LN_2) bursts to charge high-density Phase Change Material (PCM) cores and Vacuum Insulated Panels (VIP). - Triple-Vector IoT Telemetry Engine: An ultra-low-power, cloud-connected sensor matrix tracking real-time Temperature, Relative Humidity, and Oxygen (O_2) levels to ensure absolute data transparency and regulatory compliance (HSA/FDA standards). The successful candidate will contribute to prototype development, laboratory research, system integration, cold box temperature analysis, field validation at mimic cold storage environment, and technology commercialisation. [What you will be working on] - Perform 3D CAD modelling, understand basic fluid dynamics, and heat exchanger design to eliminate thermal dead zones and maximize LN_2 thermodynamic efficiency across a 1\"m\" ^3 volume. - Design, route, and balance high-pressure LN_2 cryogenic pipelines, vacuum-jacketed tubings, manifolds, and automated valve safety systems. - Build IOT, test, and integrate low-power microcontrollers and sensor arrays (Temp,RH,O_2) with live, cloud-based telemetry dashboards. - Perform laboratory experiments, cold storage environment trials, temperature and humidity monitoring, passive cold storage box testing, and data analysis.\u00a0 - Develop, integrate, and evaluate prototype systems, sensors, and instrumentation.\u00a0 - Collaborate with industry partners to support technology validation and deployment.\u00a0 - Supervise final-year project students and interns involved in the project.\u00a0 - Support intellectual property (IP) development, technology transfer, and commercialisation activities.\u00a0 - Prepare technical reports, journal publications, presentations, and research grant proposals.\u00a0 - Manage laboratory equipment & consumables, procurement, safety compliance, and research products. [What we are looking for] - Qualification in Mechanical Engineering, Thermal/Fluid Engineering, Mechatronics, Electrical & Electronic Engineering, Systems Engineering, Materials Science, or a related discipline. - Have basic foundational understanding of thermodynamics, fluid dynamics, heat transfer, or cold-chain storage technologies. - Proficiency in 3D CAD modelling (Autodesk Fusion 360 or SolidWorks) and Design for Manufacturing (DFM) principles. - Practical skills in embedded electronics, microcontroller programming (Arduino / ESP32), and IoT sensor integration. - Experience or have interest in cryogenic fluids (LN_2), heat exchangers, or fluid pipeline design is a major advantage. - A hands-on, proactive mindset with the drive to build physical prototypes and lead projects independently in a dynamic lab environment. - Strong technical writing and data presentation skills. - Entry-level candidates with strong final-year project experience in thermal fluids, mechatronics, or smart hardware are highly encouraged to apply."}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Engineering--Lecturer-Engineering-_JR-10000051375": {"title": "School of Engineering - Lecturer (Engineering)", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] School of Engineering - (Lecturer Engineering) [What you will be working on] \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Facilitate student learning, develop curriculum, and participate in development projects in Project Management related areas such as Engineering, Construction, Facilities Management, Manufacturing, and Service Industries. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Develop and conduct Continuing Education and Training (CET) lessons. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Selected candidates are also expected to take part in R&D/Implementation projects and provide consultancy services to the industry. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Duties also include mentoring students, supervising student final year projects, soliciting and supervising student internship and reaching out to various stakeholders such as secondary school students, teachers, parents and universities. [What we are looking for] \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Qualification in Engineering / Project Management / Construction Management / Facilities Management / Built Environment disciplines or equivalent. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Relevant working experience in project management of engineering or built environment projects, including planning, scheduling, resource management, and stakeholder engagement. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Strong industry linkages in project management and/or facilities management sectors. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Preferably equipped with professional certifications (e.g., PMP, CAPM) and knowledge of emerging technologies (AI in project management, digital twins, IoT-enabled facilities). \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Genuine interest and passion to share knowledge and interact with youths. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Possess sound planning, organising and multi-tasking skills, with a strong sense of commitment and responsibility for completing assigned tasks on time. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Strong communication and interpersonal skills."}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Hospitality---Associate-Lecturer--Continuing-Education---Training-_JR-10000044158": {"title": "School of Hospitality - Associate Lecturer (Continuing Education & Training)", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\nPart time\n\n[What the role is] School of Hospitality - Associate Lecturer (Continuing Education & Training) [What you will be working on] \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Deliver planned curriculum to adult learners in continuing education training (CET) programmes on scheduled weekdays, weeknights or occasional weekends. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Facilitate students\u2019 learning, perform assessment grading, and other academic duties such as invigilation. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Deliver and update of training materials, including manuals, guides and instructional videos. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Maintain accurate training records and provide regular reports to management on training outcomes and areas of improvement. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Perform curriculum development, lesson design, course delivery and module(s) supervision roles in at least two of the following subject areas: o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Mental and Workplace Wellness o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Gen AI in Hospitality o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Revenue Optimization and Management o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Service Quality and Customer Experience o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Aesthetics, Wellness and Spa Operations and Management\u00a0 [What we are looking for] \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0At least 8-10 years of relevant industry experience in hospitality, education, marketing, business development and/or consultancy. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0High-level written and verbal communication skills. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Experience supporting and working with cross-functional teams in a dynamic environment. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Strong industry links and exposures in related industry and sectors. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Experience in developing a curriculum or providing training in a client-facing environment. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Applicants with WSQ Advanced Certificate in Learning and Performance (ACLP) and the WSQ Diploma in Design and Development of Learning for Performance (DDDLP) accreditation would be an advantage. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0 As some runs of the Aesthetics, Wellness and Spa programmes are conducted in Mandarin for Mandarin-speaking participants, candidates proficient in Mandarin are welcome to apply."}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Hospitality---Associate-Lecturer--Events---Project-Management-_JR-10000052583": {"title": "School of Hospitality - Associate Lecturer (Events & Project Management)", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\nPart time\n\n[What the role is] Republic Polytechnic is seeking experienced industry practitioners to join the Diploma in Events & Project Management (DEPM) as Associate Lecturers. Associate Lecturers play an important role in bringing current industry practices, emerging trends and real-world insights into the classroom. We welcome professionals with expertise in event management, project management, experience design, event technology, digital transformation and related fields to contribute to the development of future-ready event and project management professionals. [What you will be working on] Teaching and Facilitation \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Facilitate learning for Pre-Employment Training (PET) and/or Continuing Education & Training (CET) learners. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Deliver lessons, workshops and learning activities based on approved lesson plans and curriculum materials. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Facilitate classroom discussions, project work, case studies and experiential learning activities. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Assess learners\u2019 performance through grading, feedback and evaluation of assignments, presentations and projects. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Maintain accurate records of learner attendance, participation and assessment outcomes. \u00a0 Industry Knowledge Sharing \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Share relevant industry practices, trends, technologies and case studies to enhance learners\u2019 understanding of the profession. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Provide practical insights and examples drawn from professional experience. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Support learners in understanding current and emerging developments within the events, project management and experience economy sectors. \u00a0 Learner Support \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Provide consultation and guidance to learners on assignments, projects and professional development. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Foster an engaging and inclusive learning environment that encourages participation and collaboration. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Support learner development through constructive feedback and mentorship. \u00a0 Academic Support \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Participate in lesson briefings, moderation exercises and curriculum review discussions, where required. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Provide feedback on curriculum relevance and industry developments to support continuous programme enhancement. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Support assessment and invigilation duties, where assigned. \u00a0 Areas of Expertise Applicants should possess expertise in one or more of the following areas: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Event and MICE Management \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Conference and Exhibition Management \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Event Operations and Production \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Entertainment and Live Events \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Project Management \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Customer Experience and Experience Design \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Sponsorship and Business Development \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Event Marketing and Communications \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Event Technology and Digital Experiences \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Data Analytics and Business Intelligence \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Sustainability and ESG in Events \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Artificial Intelligence and Digital Transformation \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Innovation and Design Thinking [What we are looking for] Qualifications \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Relevant tertiary qualification in Events Management, Hospitality, Tourism, Business, Marketing, Communications, Project Management or related disciplines. Industry Experience \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Minimum 5 years of relevant industry experience. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Current or recent industry practice in a relevant field will be highly advantageous. Preferred Competencies \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Strong communication and presentation skills. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Ability to engage and inspire youths and adult learners. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Passion for sharing industry knowledge and professional experiences. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Strong interpersonal and stakeholder management skills. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Ability to relate theoretical concepts to real-world applications. AI and Digital Competencies Applicants with experience in applying technology and AI within professional settings will be highly regarded. Examples include: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0AI-assisted productivity and content creation \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Digital marketing technologies \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Workflow automation tools \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Event technology platforms \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Data analytics and reporting tools \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Customer engagement technologies \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Digital transformation initiatives Commitment Associate Lecturers are typically engaged on a part-time basis and may be required to conduct minimum 2 classes during weekdays, evenings and/or weekends, depending on programme requirements."}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Hospitality---Associate-Lecturer--Hotel---Leisure-Management--F-B_JR-10000047571": {"title": "School of Hospitality - Associate Lecturer (Hotel & Leisure Management) F&B", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\nPart time\n\n[What the role is] School of Hospitality - Associate Lecturer (Hotel & Leisure Management) Food & Beverage [What you will be working on] We are seeking a dedicated and service-oriented Associate Lecturer to join our School of Hospitality, with a focus on delivering practical and industry-relevant training in Food & Beverage (F&B) Operations. This role is ideal for hospitality professionals with strong hands-on experience in restaurant, bar, or banquet operations who are passionate about developing the next generation of F&B talent. [What we are looking for] Qualifications & Experience: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0A relevant academic qualification in hospitality, hotel management, or related fields. A diploma or degree is acceptable. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0At least 5 to 8 years of industry experience in Food & Beverage Operations (e.g., restaurant, banqueting, bar, or caf\u00e9 management) within hotels, resorts, or hospitality venues. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Strong knowledge of front-of-house operations, service standards, and F&B systems (e.g. POS, inventory, reservations). \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Strong interest in hospitality education and a willingness to support student development both in and out of the classroom. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Prior experience conducting training or mentoring in a hospitality setting is an advantage. Teaching & Professional Skills: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Ability to deliver lessons in areas such as F&B Service or other service-centric modules. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Good communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to engage learners in a practical and approachable manner. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Willingness to assist in curriculum enhancement, student assessments, and hands-on practical training. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Comfortable using digital tools and technology in a teaching or demonstration environment (e.g., videos, POS software simulations). \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0A collaborative and professional approach to working with academic teams and industry partners."}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Singapore/School-of-Hospitality---Lecturer--Diploma-in-Restaurant---Culinary-Operations-_JR-10000004210": {"title": "School of Hospitality - Lecturer (Restaurant and Culinary Management)", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] You will develop curriculum and deliver training programmes based on current industry practices as well as assess students\u2019 performance as individuals and as part of a team. You are also expected to provide support to students through coaching and mentoring. In addition, you will be required to participate in research, industry projects, and diploma related events and activities. \u00a0 [What you will be working on] You will develop, review and deliver pre-employment training and continuing education curriculum related to one or more of the expertise listed below: \u2022 Restaurant Development and Entrepreneurship \u2022 Food and Beverage Management \u2022 Pastry & Baking, Food Sustainability and Food Waste Management \u2022 \u00a0Food Science R&D \u2022 F&B Technology (Restaurant Digitalisation, Data Management and Analytics) \u2022 F&B Social Media Management and Marketing \u2022 F&B Customer Journey Mapping Other supporting duties include general administration and procurement.\u00a0 Lecturers will also be required to develop and deliver training for adult learners in the continuing education space, which may take place after working hours. [What we are looking for] \u2022 At least 8 years of relevant industry experience in the areas of expertise required above.\u00a0 \u2022 Excellent oral and written communication skills in dealing with people of all levels.\u00a0 \u2022 Familiar with Singapore and regional F&B industry.\u00a0 \u2022 Experience supporting and working with cross-functional teams in a dynamic environment.\u00a0 \u2022 Good written, communication and presentation skills\u00a0 \u2022 Proficient in Microsoft Office applications, including Word, Excel and PowerPoint\u00a0 \u2022 A self-starter, agile learner and take personal interest in coaching and mentoring others.\u00a0 \u2022 Experience in developing a curriculum or providing training in a client-facing environment will be an advantage."}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Hospitality---Lecturer--Hotel---Leisure-Mgt-_JR-10000042271": {"title": "School of Hospitality - Lecturer (Hotel & Leisure Management \u2013 Front Office)", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] School of Hospitality - Lecturer (Hotel & Leisure Management - Front Office) [What you will be working on] We are looking for a dedicated and service-oriented Lecturer to join our School of Hospitality. The successful candidate will support curriculum delivery in Hotel and Leisure Management, with a strong focus on Front Office (FOH) Operations. You will play an important role in equipping students with practical skills and service excellence standards needed for frontline hospitality roles. This role is ideal for professionals with hands-on operational experience who are passionate about nurturing the next generation of hospitality talent. [What we are looking for] Qualifications & Experience: \u2022 A relevant academic qualification in hospitality, hotel management, or related fields. A diploma or degree is acceptable. \u2022 At least 5 to 8 years of industry experience in Front Office operations within hotels, resorts, or hospitality venues. \u2022 Solid understanding of guest service standards and hotel systems (e.g., PMS, TMS). \u2022 Strong interest in hospitality education and a willingness to support student development both in and out of the classroom. \u2022 Prior experience conducting training or mentoring in a hospitality setting is an advantage. Teaching & Professional Skills: \u2022 Ability to deliver lessons in areas such as Front Office Operations, Guest Relations, or other service-centric modules. \u2022 Good communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to engage learners in a practical and approachable manner. \u2022 Willingness to assist in curriculum enhancement, student assessments, and hands-on practical training. \u2022 Comfortable using digital tools and technology in a teaching or demonstration environment (e.g., videos, PMS/TMS software simulations). \u2022 A collaborative and professional approach to working with academic teams and industry partners."}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Hospitality---Lecturer-Senior-Lecturer--Events---Project-Management-_JR-10000038281-1": {"title": "School of Hospitality - Lecturer (Events & Project Management)", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] Republic Polytechnic is seeking passionate and industry-experienced professionals to join the Diploma in Events & Project Management (DEPM). We are looking for individuals who are committed to developing future-ready graduates equipped with competencies in event management, project leadership, experience design, digital transformation, sustainability, and Artificial Intelligence (AI). As a Lecturer, you will play a pivotal role in shaping the next generation of event and project management professionals equipped with versatile strategic and operational competencies. Your responsibilities extend beyond teaching to encompass nurturing students' potential, curriculum innovation, industry engagement, consultancy projects, and applied learning initiatives. [What you will be working on] Teaching and Learning Facilitate learning for Pre-Employment Training (PET) and Continuing Education & Training (CET) programmes in areas such as: Curriculum Development \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Design, develop and review curriculum, learning resources and assessments to ensure industry relevance and alignment with emerging workforce needs. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Integrate industry practices, digital technologies and AI-enabled tools into teaching and learning. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Develop authentic, industry-based learning experiences that enhance students\u2019 employability and professional competencies. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Contribute to the development of stackable credentials, professional certifications and lifelong learning programmes. Industry Engagement and Applied Learning \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Establish and maintain strong partnerships with industry stakeholders, professional associations and government agencies. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Initiate and manage industry projects, consultancy engagements and work-integrated learning opportunities. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Mentor students participating in competitions, industry showcases and experiential learning activities. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Facilitate industry visits, guest lectures and networking opportunities. AI and Digital Innovation \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Champion the adoption of AI and emerging technologies within teaching, learning and industry projects. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Guide students in the responsible and effective use of AI tools for project planning, event operations, marketing, content creation, stakeholder engagement and data analysis. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Explore and integrate emerging technologies such as Generative AI, Agentic AI, workflow automation, data analytics and digital experience platforms where relevant. Student Development \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Mentor and support students in their academic, professional and personal development. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Supervise internships, final-year projects and industry-based assignments. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Foster the development of leadership, communication, collaboration and problem-solving skills. Professional and Institutional Contributions \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Contribute to consultancy, applied research and capability development initiatives. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Design and deliver professional development programmes and customised training solutions for industry partners. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Participate in school-wide and institution-wide projects, committees and strategic initiatives. [What we are looking for] \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Relevant tertiary qualification in Events Management, Project Management, Hospitality, Tourism, Business, Marketing, Communications or a related discipline. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Postgraduate qualifications will be an advantage. Industry Experience \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Minimum 8 years of relevant industry experience in one or more of the following areas: o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0MICE and Business Events o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Conferences and Exhibitions o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Event Production and Live Events o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Project Management o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Customer Experience and Experience Design o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Event Technology and Digital Experiences o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Marketing and Communications o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Tourism and Destination Management Professional Competencies \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Strong industry knowledge and practical experience in event and project management. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Experience leading cross-functional projects and managing multiple stakeholders. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Excellent communication, presentation and facilitation skills. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Strong interpersonal skills with the ability to build and maintain industry partnerships. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Passion for coaching, mentoring and developing youths and adult learners. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Self-motivated, adaptable and committed to continuous learning. AI and Digital Competencies Candidates should demonstrate an interest in, and practical application of, technology and AI within professional settings. Experience in any of the following areas will be advantageous: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0AI-assisted productivity and collaboration tools \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Workflow automation platforms \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Digital marketing technologies \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Data analytics and visualisation tools \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Customer relationship management (CRM) platforms \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Event technology and engagement solutions \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Digital transformation initiatives"}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Hospitality---Lecturer-Senior-Lecturer_JR-10000042269": {"title": "School of Hospitality - Lecturer/Senior Lecturer", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] We are seeking a dynamic and passionate individual to join RP as a Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in the School of Hospitality. In this pivotal role which goes beyond teaching and facilitating learning, you will foster the aspirations of individual students and nurture their lifelong learning needs. Your dedication and expertise will contribute to shaping their educational journey and preparing them for future success. You are expected to conduct academic research by way of detailed observations, analyses findings, interpretation of results for potential applications and publish papers on the completed studies in peer-reviewed, well-respected journals and/or educational conferences. [What you will be working on] \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Foster a nurturing environment for students through comprehensive pastoral care and offer guidance and support in their educational and career journeys. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Develop and review module curriculum with engaging learning activities that align with the prescribed programme and module outcomes for both pre-employment training (PET) and continuing education and training (CET). \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Deliver lessons effectively through good class management and with efficacious outcomes. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Supervise students in projects and other curricular activities.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Conduct academic/action research projects to continuously develop and deepen competencies in teaching and learning. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Undertake administrative duties and academic affairs related to a programme.\u00a0 [What we are looking for] \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Possess excellent interpersonal, communication, management, and writing skills. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Demonstrate resourcefulness as a team player while exhibiting trustworthiness, independence, and a proactive work ethic. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Strong conceptual thinking skills with an ability to problem solve and recommend solutions. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Able to facilitate classroom discussions, adeptly mediate different opinions and evaluate reasoning. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Able to introduce effective interventions by analysing students' results and performance. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Preferably with academic research experience, publication, and successful funding/grant applications.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Digital literacy (using information ethically and effectively), and the ability to collaborate and communicate using digital tools. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0AI literacy that includes AI fundamentals, data science, AI tools and automation, Natural Language Processing (NLP), AI ethics, and prompt engineering. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0A minimum of five years of teaching experience, preferably teaching subjects in any of the following areas:\u00a0 >\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Hospitality Business Management >\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Customer Experience Management >\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Customer Journey Mapping and Analytics"}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Hospitality---Senior-Lecturer--Capabilities---Industry-Development-_JR-10000054835": {"title": "School of Hospitality - Senior Lecturer (Capabilities & Industry Development)", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] School of Hospitality - Senior Lecturer (Capabilities & Industry Development) [What you will be working on] The School of Hospitality is seeking an experienced hospitality professional with expertise in hotel management, business development, and tech & innovation. The successful candidate will contribute to teaching and learning, drive hospitality transformation projects, develop strategic partnerships, and lead initiatives that enhance industry capabilities through technology and innovation. Teaching & Learning \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Teach and facilitate learning in hospitality-related modules, including hotel operations, guest experience management, hospitality technology, and service innovation. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Develop and review curriculum to ensure alignment with evolving industry needs and emerging technologies. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Mentor and supervise students in projects, internships, and industry-based learning activities. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Integrate industry practices, digital tools, and experiential learning approaches into teaching and assessment. Hospitality & Digital Innovation Projects \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Lead industry projects and consultancy initiatives focused on hotel operations, guest experience, and hospitality transformation. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Drive the adoption and application of emerging hospitality technologies, including Artificial Intelligence, data analytics and business intelligence, smart hotel and Internet of Things solutions, Property Management Systems, Customer Relationship Management platforms, and contactless guest experience technologies. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Identify, develop, and implement innovative solutions that enhance operational efficiency, service quality, and customer experience. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Manage hospitality innovation and capability-development projects, including project planning, stakeholder engagement, resource coordination, risk management, and delivery of project outcomes. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Conduct applied research and collaborate with industry partners to address business challenges and support workforce transformation. Business Development & Industry Engagement \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Build and maintain partnerships with hotels, hospitality organisations, technology providers, and government agencies. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Identify and secure opportunities for consultancy, executive education, applied research, and collaborative industry projects. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Develop proposals, business cases, and partnership agreements. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Represent the School at industry forums, conferences, and networking events. [What we are looking for] \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Relevant qualification(s) in Hospitality Management, Hotel Administration, Tourism, Business, Information Systems, Digital Transformation, or a related discipline. A postgraduate qualification is advantageous. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0At least 8 years of relevant industry experience in hotel management, hospitality consulting, hospitality technology, tourism, or a related sector. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Strong understanding of hotel operations and hospitality technologies. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Experience in hospitality digital transformation, smart hospitality solutions, AI applications, service innovation, or customer experience enhancement. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Proven track record in business development, industry engagement, and partnership management. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Strong project leadership and stakeholder management skills. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Excellent communication, presentation, facilitation, and relationship-building abilities. Preferred Attributes \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Passion for hospitality innovation and digital transformation. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Strong industry network within the hospitality and tourism sectors. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Ability to bridge industry practice with applied education and research. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Self-motivated, adaptable, and collaborative team player."}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Infocomm---Associate-Lecturer--Cybersecurity---Digital-Forensics-_JR-10000054099": {"title": "School of Infocomm \u2013 Associate Lecturer (Cybersecurity & Digital Forensics)", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\nPart time\n\n[What the role is] School of Infocomm \u2013 Associate Lecturer (Cybersecurity & Digital Forensics) [What you will be working on] You will be involved in the following to support our full time and part-time course offerings in areas related to Penetration Testing/Red Teaming, Web Application and Cloud Security, SOC Operations, IT Audit & Compliance, Digital Forensics, and other foundational ICT modules. \u2022 Implement and administer module delivery, related activities (including student assessments and assignments) to meet learning outcomes. \u2022 Deliver module curriculum, learning activities and materials. \u2022 Stay current and responsive to changing developments in the profession and educational landscape. \u2022 Maintain links with industry to stay current and to promote collaborations. [What we are looking for] Applicants should have a relevant qualification preferably in the fields of IT/Computer Science, with a minimum of 1 year's industry experience. Industry certifications such as CISSP, CISA, CISM, CEH and OSCP will be a plus.\u00a0 Applicants should be proficient in two or more of the following areas:\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Penetration Testing/Red Teaming \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0SOC operations, Firewall Configuration\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Cloud Security, Web Application Security\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0IT Audit and Compliance, Personal Data Protection\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Digital Forensics"}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Singapore/School-of-Infocomm---Lecturer--Cloud-Native-Infrastructure-_JR-10000032815": {"title": "School of Infocomm - Lecturer (Cloud Native Infrastructure)", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] School of Infocomm - Lecturer (Cloud Native Infrastructure) [What you will be working on] The school is looking for dynamic individuals with a high degree of self-motivation and the ability to work effectively in a team environment. You will be involved in the following to support our full time and part-time course offerings in areas related cloud native infrastructure and foundational ICT modules. \u2022 Implement and administer module delivery, related activities (including student assessments and assignments) to meet learning outcomes.\u00a0 \u2022 Plan, design and develop module curriculum, learning activities and materials.\u00a0 \u2022 Stay current and responsive to changing developments in the profession and educational landscape through active engagement with industry and professional bodies/communities. \u2022 Maintain links with industry to stay current and to promote collaborations. You will have the opportunity to develop and grow your capabilities through industry projects or academic research projects and professional learning communities. [What we are looking for] Applicants should have a relevant qualification preferably in the fields of Computer Science/Engineering, with a minimum of 1 year\u2019s industry experience. Industry certifications such as CCNA, RHCSA, Azure, AWS, DevOps will be a plus.\u00a0 Applicants should be proficient in two or more of the following areas:\u00a0 \u2022 Scripting languages such as Python, Powershell, Bash \u2022 Cloud Operations in DevOps with Continuous Integration and Continuous Deployment (CI/CD) \u2022 Infrastructure Automation for configuration and management e.g. Ansible/ Chef / Puppet \u2022 Monitoring and working with large data using APM tools e.g. Splunk / Elk stack \u2022 Container Management / Orchestration, e.g. Kubernetes / Docker Swarm/ Portman \u2022 Administration of Private Cloud Infrastructure e.g. VMWare / OpenStack and Public Cloud Infrastructure e.g. AWS / Azure / Google \u2022 Administration skills in Data Centre / Enterprise Networking, Linux and Windows servers"}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Singapore/School-of-Infocomm---Lecturer--Common-Infocomm-Programme-_JR-10000028692": {"title": "School of Infocomm - Lecturer (Common Infocomm Programme)", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] School of Infocomm - Lecturer (Common Infocomm Programme) [What you will be working on] The school is looking for dynamic individuals with a high degree of self-motivation and the ability to work effectively in a team environment.\u00a0 You will be involved in the following to support our full-time and part-time course offerings in areas related to software development, computer systems and networks, artificial intelligence and other foundational ICT modules. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Implement and administer module delivery, related activities (including student assessments and assignments) to meet learning outcomes.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Plan, design and develop module curriculum, learning activities and materials.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Stay current and responsive to changing developments in the profession and educational landscape through active engagement with industry and professional bodies/communities. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Maintain links with industry to stay current and to promote collaborations. You will have the opportunities to develop and grow your capabilities through industry projects or academic research projects and professional learning communities. [What we are looking for] Applicants should have a relevant qualification preferably in the fields of IT/Computer Science, with a minimum of 1 year\u2019s industry experience. Applicants should be proficient in two or more of the following areas: \u2022 Programming (e.g. Python, Javascript, React, Node.js, PWA) \u2022 Agile software development \u2022 Cyber-security and Cloud infrastructure \u2022 Data science, Machine Learning & Artificial Intelligence"}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Infocomm---Lecturer--Data-Analytics---Machine-Learning-_JR-10000041058": {"title": "School of Infocomm - Lecturer (Artificial Intelligence/Machine Learning)", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] The school is looking for dynamic individuals who are motivated and able to work effectively in a team environment. [What you will be working on] As a Lecturer in Artificial Intelligence (AI), you will shape the next generation of AI professionals. This role contributes to a field transforming industries. You will impart knowledge in AI, machine learning (ML), and deep learning (DL), covering how machines simulate human intelligence in learning, comprehension, creativity, and problem-solving. Professionals fitting various AI job descriptions are in high demand across sectors including IT, education, finance, and healthcare. Your core responsibilities will involve designing, developing, and delivering curriculum, as well as supervising practical projects. You will teach AI, ML, DL, and generative AI. This includes: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Teaching AI models to learn from data for applications like chatbots, self-driving cars, and voice recognition. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Guiding students in building data science infrastructure, data preprocessing, and cleansing. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Planning for deployment into production environments. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Supervising projects involving speech recognition, data mining, and advanced robotics. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Collaborating with experts and communicating AI utility to diverse audiences. \u00a0 [What we are looking for] We seek a skilled, innovative professional passionate about AI/ML, dedicated to fostering student career growth and establishing strong industry connections. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Education: A Bachelor\u2019s degree in Computer Science, Data Science, Artificial Intelligence, or a related field. A Master\u2019s or Ph.D. in Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning, or Data Science is highly preferred. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Experience: At least 1-year relevant experience as an AI Specialist, Data Scientist, Machine Learning Engineer, or similar AI development role is crucial. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Certifications: Relevant AI/ML certifications (e.g., Microsoft Certified: Azure AI Fundamentals, AWS Certified Machine Learning, Google AI Certification) are beneficial. Key Skills: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Technical Proficiency: Strong grasp of programming languages such as Python, Flutter, and C++; good knowledge of linear algebra, calculus, statistics, and probability. Extensive experience with ML frameworks like PyTorch, TensorFlow, and Keras, and various ML/deep learning algorithms. Proficiency in cloud platforms for AI deployment (AWS, Azure, Google Cloud), and strong understanding of data modeling, mining, and processing. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Soft Skills: Excellent problem-solving and analytical skills; strong communication and collaboration abilities to work effectively in teams; adaptability to new AI developments; and understanding of AI ethics, data privacy, and bias. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Genuine passion to share knowledge, mentor and interact with youths and adult learners, with strong pastoral and interpersonal skills."}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Singapore/School-of-Infocomm---Lecturer--Digital-Design---Development-_JR-10000004218": {"title": "School of Infocomm - Lecturer (Software Development / Full Stack Development)", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] The school is looking for dynamic individuals with a high degree of self-motivation and the ability to work effectively in a team environment. [What you will be working on] You will be involved in the following to support our full time and part-time course offerings in areas related to Software Development, Full Stack Development, and other foundational ICT modules. \u2022 Implement and administer module delivery, related activities (including student assessments and assignments) to meet learning outcomes. \u2022 Plan, design and develop module curriculum, learning activities and materials. \u2022 Stay current and responsive to changing developments in the profession and educational landscape through active engagement with industry and professional bodies/communities. \u2022 Maintain links with industry to stay current and to promote collaborations. You will have the opportunities to develop and grow your capabilities through industry projects or academic research projects and professional learning communities. [What we are looking for] Applicants should have a relevant qualification in IT / Computer Science, with a minimum of 1 year\u2019s industry experience. Applicants should be proficient in two or more of the following areas: \u2022 Programming languages such as Python, JavaScript ES6 \u2022 Development of mobile and web applications and software testing \u2022 UI/UX design for software development \u2022 Containerization platforms and/or cloud deployment technologies \u2022 Application deployment by using CI/CD"}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Infocomm---Lecturer--FinTech-_JR-10000053212": {"title": "School of Infocomm \u2013 Lecturer (FinTech)", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] The School of Infocomm is looking for dynamic individuals with a high degree of self-motivation and the ability to work effectively in a team environment. You will be involved in supporting our full-time and part-time course offerings in areas related to Financial Technology (FinTech), Artificial Intelligence (AI), Data Analytics, Digital Payments, Financial Systems, Automation, Blockchain Technologies, and other foundational ICT modules. [What you will be working on] Implement and administer module delivery and related activities (including student assessments and assignments) to achieve learning outcomes. Plan, design and develop curriculum, learning activities and teaching materials. Stay current and responsive to developments in AI, FinTech, and the broader technology and education landscape through active engagement with industry and professional communities. Maintain strong industry links to ensure curriculum relevance and foster collaborations with industry partners. Contribute to applied research, consultancy, innovation projects, and industry partnerships in areas related to AI, FinTech, digital transformation, and emerging technologies. Support student learning, career development, internships, industry projects, and other experiential learning opportunities. You will have opportunities to develop and grow your capabilities through industry projects, academic research, professional learning communities, and collaborative initiatives with industry partners. [What we are looking for] Applicants should possess relevant qualifications, preferably in Computer Science, Information Technology, Financial Technology, Data Science, Artificial Intelligence, Software Engineering, or related disciplines, with a minimum of 2 years of industry experience. Applicants should be proficient in one or more of the following areas: Artificial Intelligence (AI), Generative AI, Agentic AI, Machine Learning, Data Analytics, or Intelligent Automation. Digital Payments, Financial Systems, Open Banking, Embedded Finance, RegTech, Financial Crime Technologies, or related FinTech domains. Programming languages and frameworks such as Python, Java, Spring, JavaScript, Node.js, or related technologies. Blockchain technologies, including distributed ledger concepts, smart contracts, decentralised applications, and relevant blockchain platforms, alongside modern software development practices such as APIs, DevOps, CI/CD, and application development. Implementation experience in the FinTech, AI, data analytics, digital transformation, or software development industries. Preferred Attributes Genuine passion for teaching, knowledge sharing, and mentoring youths and adult learners. Strong pastoral care, communication, and interpersonal skills, with the ability to inspire and engage learners from diverse backgrounds. Dedicated to fostering students\u2019 personal, academic, and career growth, while helping them build industry-relevant skills and professional networks. Ability to establish and maintain strong industry partnerships to support internships, industry projects, applied research, and employment opportunities for students. Passion for lifelong learning and staying current with emerging trends in AI, FinTech, digital transformation, and technology innovation."}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Singapore/School-of-Infocomm---Lecturer--Infocomm-Security-Management-_JR-10000004212": {"title": "School of Infocomm - Lecturer (Cybersecurity & Digital Forensics)", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] The school is looking for dynamic individuals with a high degree of self-motivation and the ability to work effectively in a team environment. [What you will be working on] You will be involved in the following to support our full time and part-time course offerings in areas related to Penetration Testing/Red Teaming, Web Application and Cloud Security, SOC Operations, IT Audit & Compliance, Digital Forensics, and other foundational ICT modules. \u2022 Implement and administer module delivery, related activities (including student assessments and assignments) to meet learning outcomes. \u2022 Plan, design and develop module curriculum, learning activities and materials. \u2022 Stay current and responsive to changing developments in the profession and educational landscape through active engagement with industry and professional bodies/communities. \u2022 Maintain links with industry to stay current and to promote collaborations. You will have the opportunities to develop and grow your capabilities through industry projects or academic research projects and professional learning communities. [What we are looking for] Applicants should have a relevant qualification preferably in the fields of IT/Computer Science, with a minimum of 1 year's industry experience. Industry certifications such as CISSP, CISA, CISM, CEH and OSCP will be a plus.\u00a0 Applicants should be proficient in two or more of the following areas:\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Penetration Testing/Red Teaming \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0SOC operations, Firewall Configuration\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Cloud Security, Web Application Security\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0IT Audit and Compliance, Personal Data Protection\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Digital Forensics"}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Singapore/School-of-Infocomm---Lecturer-Senior-Lecturer--CET-and-Skills-Future-_JR-10000027583": {"title": "School of Infocomm - Lecturer/Senior Lecturer (CET and Skills Future)", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] School of Infocomm - Lecturer/Senior Lecturer (CET and Skills Future) The school is looking for dynamic individuals with a high degree of self-motivation and the ability to work effectively in a team environment. You will be involved in making a significant impact in keeping up with RP\u2019s CET plans and future goals. [What you will be working on] \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Analyse market trends and data to propose training courses and implement marketing campaigns by utilizing insights to attract prospective applicants. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Engage with companies, tailoring CET programs to meet specific workforce upskilling requirements. Propose customization will be the bridge between corporate needs and course delivery. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Drive marketing efforts through physical events and social media initiatives. Enhance the online presence of our CET offerings, captivating both individual learners and corporate accounts alike. Business Development Responsibilities: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Corporate Partnerships: Proactively identify and reach out to potential corporate clients to build strategic partnerships. Present CET programs as solutions for corporate training and development needs. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Revenue Generation: Develop and execute business development strategies to increase revenue through corporate training partnerships. Identify opportunities for expanding the CET portfolio to meet the needs of various industries. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Client Relationship Management: Maintain and nurture relationships with corporate clients to ensure satisfaction and repeat business. Gather feedback to continuously improve program offerings. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Proposal Development & Negotiation: Lead the creation of customized training proposals and negotiate contracts with corporate clients, ensuring mutual benefit and alignment with CET objectives. As an academic staff, you will also support our full-time and part-time course offerings in areas related ICT modules. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Implement and administer module delivery, related activities (including student assessments and assignments) to meet learning outcomes.\u00a0 [What we are looking for] Applicants should have a relevant qualification in IT / Computer Science, with a minimum of 1 year industry experience. Applicants with business development or pre-sales consulting experience is preferred. Applicants should be proficient in any two or more of the following areas:\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Programming languages such as Python and/or Java. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Development of mobile and web applications and software testing. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Containerization platforms and/or cloud deployment technologies. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0IT Audit and Compliance, Personal Data Protection. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0IT Project Management / IT Product Management. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Penetration Testing / Digital Forensics. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0TensorFlow/PyTorch, DeepSpeed/Megatron-LM. LLM frameworks"}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Management-and-Communication---Lecturer--Common-Business-Programme-_JR-10000015079": {"title": "School of Business - Lecturer (Common Business Programme)", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] School of Business - Lecturer (Common Business Programme) [What you will be working on] As a Lecturer with the School of Business, you will play a key role in nurturing future-ready graduates through authentic, learner-centred education and close industry collaboration. You will be expected to: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Facilitate engaging and experiential learning using Republic Polytechnic's Problem-Based Learning (PBL) pedagogy and other learner-centred approaches. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Contribute to programme development, quality assurance, academic administration, and continuous improvement initiatives to enhance the student learning experience. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Design, develop, review, and deliver industry-relevant curricula that equip students with the knowledge, skills and competencies required by the accounting profession. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Build and sustain strong partnerships with industry to support curriculum innovation, student internships, student industry projects, and capability development initiatives. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Mentor students in their academic, career and personal development, including coaching student teams, overseeing internships, projects and supporting student life and leadership programmes. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Teach and contribute to one or more of the following areas: \u00a0 \u00a0o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Financial and Management Accounting \u00a0 \u00a0o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Audit & Assurance \u00a0 \u00a0o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Taxation \u00a0 \u00a0o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Sustainable Finance ESG & Sustainability Reporting\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0AI & Digital Technologies in Accounting \u00a0 \u00a0o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Risk, Regulatory Compliance and Corporate Governance \u00a0 \u00a0o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Business Law and Company Law [What we are looking for] \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Relevant qualifications in accounting, or a related discipline. A postgraduate qualification will be an advantage. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Professional qualifications such as ACCA, CA Singapore, ICAEW, CPA Australia or equivalent are preferred. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0At least 5 years of relevant industry experience in accounting, audit, taxation, sustainability reporting, risk management, or regulatory compliance. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Passion for developing youths and adult learners through innovative and applied learning approaches. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Strong communication, facilitation, and interpersonal skills, with the ability to engage PET students, adult learners, colleagues, and industry partners effectively. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Ability to lead projects, build industry partnerships and work collaboratively across multidisciplinary teams. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Experience in teaching, curriculum development, or training will be an advantage."}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Singapore/School-of-Management-and-Communication---Lecturer--Human-Resource-Management-with-Psychology---EG-_JR-10000004202": {"title": "School of Business - Lecturer (Human Resource Management with Psychology)", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] As part of the academic team in the Diploma in Human Resources with Psychology (DHRMP), you will play a key role in shaping the next generation of HR and career counselling professionals through applied learning and industry engagement. [What you will be working on] \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Facilitate learning for both Pre-Employment Training (PET) and Continuing Education & Training (CET) learners through interactive seminar, workshop, coaching, and experiential learning activities.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Design, review and deliver industry-relevant curriculum in areas such as:\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0Full HR functions \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 - \u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0HR Analytics & HR Technology (AI) \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 - \u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Strategic and Operational HR Functions\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 - \u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Industrial & Organisational Psychology\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 - \u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Positive Psychology\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 - \u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Psychometric Assessment\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 - \u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Socio-emotional Counselling\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Lead and supervise student-industry collaboration projects, applying real-world HR practices to authentic workplace challenges.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Partner with industry stakeholders to develop consultancy, applied research, and capability development projects.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Build and maintain strong industry networks to create meaningful opportunities for students, including mentorships, industry projects, internships, and award sponsorships.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Mentor and guide students in their academic, professional, and personal development journey.\u00a0 This role is well-suited for experienced HR, career counselling, psychology, or organisational development professionals who are keen to leverage their industry expertise to develop future HR leaders, and make a meaningful impact through education. [What we are looking for] \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Relevant qualifications in Human Resource Management, Psychology, Career Counselling, Organisational Development, or related disciplines.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Professional accreditation and/or membership with recognised bodies would be advantageous, not limiting to:\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 - \u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0NCDA credentials\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 - \u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0IHRP certification\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0At least 5 years of relevant industry experience in HR, career counselling, psychology, organisational development, or related fields.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Strong industry networks and the ability to engage organisations on applied projects, collaborations, and talent development initiatives.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Passionate about developing people and nurturing future-ready professionals.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Strong communication, stakeholder management, and project management skills, with the ability to manage multiple initiatives effectively.\u00a0 You will thrive in this role if you are looking for an opportunity to transition from industry into academia while continuing to stay connected to industry practices, contribute to workforce capability development, and influence the future of the profession."}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Sports-and-Health-Lecturer-Senior-Lecturer--Integrated-Community-Care-_JR-10000049638": {"title": "School of Sports and Health-Lecturer/Senior Lecturer (Integrated Community Care)", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] School of Sports and Health \u2013 Lecturer / Senior Lecturer (Diploma in Integrated Community Care) The School of Sports and Health, whose vision is to be a leading educator in the domains of sports, health, and community care, invites qualified and passionate candidates to apply for the position of Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in the Diploma in Integrated Community Care (DICC). [What you will be working on] The Diploma in Integrated Community Care aims to prepare students for emerging roles in Singapore\u2019s evolving health and social care landscape. The programme equips learners with competencies to support integrated care models that span healthcare, social services, and community-based support systems. The Lecturer/Senior Lecturer will: \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Deliver academic and instructional duties for both Pre-Employment Training (PET) and Continuing Education and Training (CET) programmes. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Design, review, and update curriculum to ensure relevance to the sector and uphold academic governance. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Facilitate student learning through experiential, practice-based approaches and mentor students in their holistic development. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Supervise students in final-year projects, internships, overseas study trips, and co-curricular activities. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Develop and maintain partnerships with healthcare providers, community organisations, and social service agencies to support applied learning and research. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Contribute to applied research and development projects that promote innovation in integrated community care delivery. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Take part in school-wide administrative duties, event organisation, outreach activities, and other committee roles. [What we are looking for] \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Relevant qualification in nursing, allied health, social work, public health, health administration, or a related discipline.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0At least 3\u20135 years of relevant experience in the community care or healthcare sector (e.g., aged care, primary care, integrated care settings, ILTC providers, VWOs, or public health institutions). \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Working knowledge and/or experience in areas such as: o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Integrated care models and frameworks o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Community health and social care coordination o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Gerontology and active ageing o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Health promotion and chronic disease management o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Multi-disciplinary care planning \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Familiarity with local health and social care systems and government initiatives (e.g., Healthier SG, Community Networks for Seniors) is preferred. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Passionate about education, student development, and building manpower for the integrated care sector. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Self-motivated, team-oriented, and committed to delivering high-quality teaching and project outcomes. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Strong communication, planning, and organisation skills, with attention to detail."}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Sports-and-Health-Lecturer-Senior-Lecturer--Outdoor-Education-_JR-10000053468": {"title": "School of Sports and Health-Lecturer/Senior Lecturer (Outdoor Education)", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] The School of Sports and Health invites passionate and driven individuals to join its dynamic team in advancing sports, health and outdoor education. The Diploma in Outdoor Education (DOE) team aspires to be a recognised thought leader and trusted partner in research, training and development within the outdoor education, recreation and inclusive practice sectors. [What you will be working on] Job Responsibilities The Lecturer/Senior Lecturer for the Diploma in Outdoor Education will contribute to teaching, curriculum development, student mentoring, programme delivery and industry engagement in the following areas: Deliver quality Pre-Employment Training (PET) modules and Continuing Education and Training (CET) programmes in outdoor education and related areas, including: \u2022 Climbing and Abseiling\u00a0 \u2022 Kayaking\u00a0 \u2022 Challenge Course Management \u2022 Land-based outdoor skills such as campcraft and navigation \u2022 Supervision and management\u00a0 \u2022 Instruction and Facilitation\u00a0 \u2022 Adventure and experiential education \u2022 Youth Outreach and Development\u00a0 \u2022 Environmental studies and Nature interpretation\u00a0 \u2022 Expedition Management \u2022 Demonstrate a strong commitment to holistic student development, including mentoring, guidance, and support for students\u2019 academic, personal, and professional growth. \u2022 Serve as a positive role model for students, exemplifying professionalism, integrity, care, and responsible conduct in all learning and engagement contexts. Develop, review and enhance curriculum to ensure alignment with current industry practices, applied research, safety standards and emerging trends in outdoor education. \u2022 Design and facilitate authentic, experiential and student-centred learning experiences that develop students\u2019 technical competence, confidence, leadership, resilience and reflective practice. \u2022 Uphold robust safety, risk management and operational standards during practical lessons, field-based learning, expeditions and outdoor programmes. \u2022 Build and sustain partnerships with industry, community and professional bodies to support curriculum relevance, student development, applied projects and continuing education opportunities. [What we are looking for] \u2022 Relevant qualifications in outdoor education, sports, recreation, education, health, or related discipline, with at least 5 years of relevant industry experience. \u2022 Good written and oral communication skills. \u2022 Strong time management, organisational and administrative skills, with the ability to manage multiple responsibilities and meet deadlines. \u2022 Agility to learn and adapt to changes. \u2022 Demonstrates a strong passion for outdoor education, with responsibility, reliability,\u00a0 independence, initiative in problem-solving, resourcefulness and the ability to work effectively in a team. \u2022 Strong communication and interpersonal skills to establish and maintain quality working relationships with students, colleagues, and stakeholders. \u2022 Proficient in the following methods of instruction and facilitation skills: o\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Group management skills o\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Group facilitation and review skills o\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Presentation and lecturing skills o\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Programme/game design and lesson planning skills \u2022 Preferably holds relevant certifications in outdoor and adventure skills such as: o\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Kayak Level 3 Coaching and/or o\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Climbing Instructor Category 2 and/or\u00a0 o\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Abseiling Level 3. o\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 First Aid and CPR AED certification \u2022 Experience in designing and conducting programmes for participants with disabilities, older adults or children will be an advantage."}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Technology-for-Arts--Media---Design---AD--Capability---Industry-_JR-10000054113": {"title": "School of Technology for Arts, Media & Design - AD (Capability & Industry)", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] The Assistant Director (Capability & Industry) is a strategic and hands-on leader responsible for driving consultancy, applied research, intellectual property development, and external industry engagement for the School of Technology for Arts, Media and Design. This role leads the development and execution of strategies that strengthen the School\u2019s staff capability, grow consultancy and applied research activity, and expand the School\u2019s industry relevance beyond the traditional creative sector. We are looking for individuals with the ability to lead cross-functional teams, provide leadership on complex and novel issues and shape policies, practices, and partnerships that advance the School\u2019s strategic objectives. This role is critical in positioning the School of Technology for the Arts, Media and Design as a strategic partner to industry, both within the creative sector and across the wider economy. By shaping functional priorities, building staff capability, driving applied consultancy, research, and intellectual property development, and opening new industry pathways, the Assistant Director enables the School to strengthen industry relevance, create reusable intellectual assets, and deliver meaningful, sustainable impact beyond traditional academic boundaries. [What you will be working on] Spearhead consultancy, applied research, and industry engagement initiatives to strengthen the School\u2019s industry-facing capabilities and impact. Develop and implement functional strategies, policies, and frameworks to drive sustainable growth and measurable impact. Address novel and complex challenges by integrating creative, arts, design, and media perspectives and disciplines with industry needs. Drive the identification, structuring, and delivery of consultancy and applied research projects, including opportunities to generate intellectual property particularly with non-creative industry and government partners. Identify and pursue collaborative projects with industry partners, developing tailored solutions that draw on STA\u2019s strengths in digital media solutions, immersive experiences, design-led innovation, and Designing Your Life facilitation. Enhance consultancy models, processes, and service quality by applying best practices to improve intellectual property and revenue generation, and project outcomes. Coach and mentor staff, building School-wide capability in consultancy delivery, industry-facing research, and professional practice. Lead upskilling initiatives and foster cross-disciplinary collaboration to address skill gaps. Build and maintain strategic partnerships with corporates, agencies, research institutions, and solution providers. Influence School and institutional leaders to adopt new approaches and priorities, and negotiate with external partners to achieve mutually beneficial outcomes. Work across functions and schools to align resources, manage dependencies, and optimise results, exercising autonomy and sound judgement. [What we are looking for] Relevant qualification in arts, media, design, creative technologies, business, engineering or a related discipline. Significant professional experience in business development, industry partnerships, consultancy, applied research, innovation or related industry-facing roles. Demonstrated success in capability development, consultancy growth, applied research, intellectual property development, industry engagement and stakeholder partnership development. Proven experience in translating creative or design-led strengths into industry-relevant solutions for non-Arts, Design and Media sector organizations. Experience developing or supporting tailored industry solutions in areas such as arts and digital media, immersive experiences, and related domains. Strong track record in influencing stakeholders, negotiating with external partners, and driving change across complex stakeholder environments. Ability to operate independently and confidently in complex, ambiguous and evolving environments, with sound judgement and accountability for outcomes."}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/COI-SCM---Manager-Senior-Manager_JR-10000038982": {"title": "Centre of Innovation for Supply Chain Management \u2013 Manager/Senior Manager", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-24\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] Centre of Innovation for Supply Chain Management \u2013 Manager/Senior Manager [What you will be working on] \u2022 Able to quickly understand company's logistics and supply chain capabilities to meet business needs to propose relevant consultancy and technology solutions \u2022 Execute end-to-end supply chain and logistics process review for process, digitalisation, AI, visibility, IoT and Warehouse Automation Opportunities \u2022 Implement innovative and impactful digitalisation, LEAN process and warehouse automation projects to industry\u00a0 \u2022 Support outreach events with setup and assisting in demonstrations\u00a0 [What we are looking for] Business development:\u00a0 \u2022 A driven self-starter that actively keeps abreast with business needs and can quickly put together proof-of-concepts to meet business needs\u00a0 \u2022 Sell to both business leaders and operations staff the benefits of process and technology innovation \u2022 Strong collaborator with internal and external stakeholders to execute impactful supply chain projects Familiarity in implementing:\u00a0 \u2022 Process improvement using LEAN, swimlane and other process discovery tools \u2022 practical Warehouse Automation possibilities and technology trends \u2022 Office 365 tools (including Power\u2028Automate, PowerBl, SharePoint, Power Apps, etc) and Google Workspace/ Cloud tools like Google Appsheet\u00a0 \u2022 Motivated to explore, learn and apply new technologies in warehouse automation, AI and physical AI"}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Technology-for-Arts--Media-and-Design---Assoc-Lecturer--Sonic-Arts-_JR-10000055128": {"title": "School of Technology for Arts, Media and Design - Assoc Lecturer (Sonic Arts)", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-04\nPart time\n\n[What the role is] School of Technology for Arts, Media and Design - Associate Lecturer (Sonic Arts) [What you will be working on] Associate Lecturers will: \u2022 Develop (when necessary) and teach modules such as: Live Sound, Sound Design for Games,\u00a0 Audio Post-Production, Interactive Audio, Sound for Media & Foley Arts \u2022 Supervise students in portfolio development, final year projects and internship \u00a0\u2022 Invigilate exams during two exam periods per semester (as assigned) \u2022 Develop lecturing competencies by attending training (as assigned) \u2022 Participate in lesson briefings and review sessions [What we are looking for] \u2022 Qualification preferably in the field of IT, Media and or Sound / Music Specialisation \u2022 A minimum of three years industry experience, preferably in a related field. Teaching experience is an added advantage \u2022 Must have working experience in any of, or a combination of the following areas:- Live Sound, Network Audio,\u00a0 Sound Design for Games, Audio Programming, Location Sound, Audio Post-Production and relevant broadcast standards- Operational knowledge of software such as Adobe Audition, Avid Pro Tools, Ableton Live, MaxMSP, Unity, Wwise \u2022 Able to work independently as well as in a team \u2022 Able to work within tight deadlines \u2022 Able to communicate well with students of diverse academic, socioeconomic, and cultural backgrounds. Additional advantages: \u2022 Have strong administrative skills \u2022 Have strong IT skills \u2022 Strong skills in e-learning tools and resources \u2022 Ability to teach one or more of the following modules:- Art of Story- Creative Enterprise"}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/Office-of-Digitalisation--Data-and-AI---Deputy-Manager--Data-Hub---Data-Product-_JR-10000055568": {"title": "Office of Digitalisation, Data and AI - Deputy Manager (Data Hub & Data Product)", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-15\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] The Deputy Manager, Data Hub & Data Products supports the design, development, and operationalisation of an Institute of Higher Learning (IHL) enterprise Data Hub. The role combines capabilities in data architecture, data modelling, and data product management to ensure data assets are organised, governed and delivered as trusted data products that support analytics, reporting, AI and decision-making. The incumbent will work closely with Schools, Departments, business stakeholders, and external technology vendors to translate business requirements into scalable enterprise data models and data products. [What you will be working on] 1. Data Product Management \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Support the development and delivery of enterprise data products aligned with IHL's strategic priorities. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Work with business stakeholders to understand business needs, data requirements and desired outcomes. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Translate business use cases into data product requirements, user stories and delivery roadmaps. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Prioritise data product improvements based on business value and institutional impact. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Drive adoption and usage of Data Hub data products across the institute. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Monitor data product performance, usage and business outcomes. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Support the implementation of Data-as-a-Service (DaaS) capabilities. 2. Enterprise Data Modelling \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Design and maintain conceptual, logical and physical data models for enterprise-wide data domains. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Develop scalable data models that support analytics, operational reporting and AI use cases. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Define and maintain business entities, relationships, business rules and metadata. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Ensure consistency and alignment of data definitions across systems and domains. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Support the development of enterprise semantic models and reusable datasets. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Collaborate with Data Owners and Data Stewards to establish trusted data definitions. 3. Data Architecture and Integration \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Support the Lead Data Architect in designing enterprise data architecture and target-state Data Hub architecture. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Review solution designs proposed by vendors and ensure alignment with enterprise architecture principles and standards. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Support data ingestion, transformation, integration and data lifecycle design activities. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Assess scalability, performance, maintainability and usability of architecture solutions. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Contribute to enterprise data architecture blueprints, standards and reference architectures. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Ensure effective integration across enterprise applications, learning systems and analytics platforms. 4. Data Warehouse and Data Hub Delivery \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Lead technical discussions relating to design and implementation. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Review ETL/ELT pipelines, data transformation logic and data quality processes. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Support onboarding of new source systems into the Data Hub. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Identify data quality, performance and integration issues and coordinate resolution efforts. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Support testing, validation and release activities for Data Hub initiatives. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Ensure data assets are AI-ready, reusable and scalable. 5. Vendor and Technical Management \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Provide day-to-day oversight of external vendors delivering Data Hub solutions. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Review vendor deliverables, technical documentation and implementation approaches. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Challenge proposed designs where necessary and ensure solutions meet business requirements. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Perform root cause analysis of data-related issues and coordinate resolution. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Be hands-on in investigating data pipeline failures, integration issues, data discrepancies and performance bottlenecks. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Escalate delivery, architecture or quality issues when required. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Ensure knowledge transfer and documentation are completed by vendors. [What we are looking for] \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Qualification in Information Systems, Computer Science, Data Analytics, Data Engineering or related discipline. Experience \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0At least 5 years of experience in: o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Data Warehousing o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Enterprise Data Management o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Data Architecture o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Data Modelling o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Data Engineering o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Business Intelligence or Analytics Platforms \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Experience delivering enterprise-scale data platforms. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Experience managing vendors and technology implementation projects. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Experience working in education, public sector or large complex organisations is advantageous. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Familiarity with IHL business processes and data domains is highly desirable. Knowledge & Skills \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Strong knowledge of:\u00a0 o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Data Warehousing concepts o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Dimensional Modelling o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Star and Snowflake Schemas o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Modern data architecture principles o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0ETL / ELT design o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Master and Reference Data Management o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Metadata Management o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Data Quality Management o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Microsoft Fabric, Azure Data Services \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Ability to communicate effectively with both technical and non-technical stakeholders. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Strong facilitation, negotiation and influencing skills. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Ability to bridge business, technology and data teams."}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/Office-of-Digitalisation--Data-and-AI---Deputy-Manager-Manager--Data-Scientist-_JR-10000052242": {"title": "Office of Digitalisation, Data and AI - Deputy Manager (Data and AI Governance)", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-15\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] The Deputy Manager, Data & AI Governance is responsible for developing, maintaining, and operationalising Institute of Higher Learning (IHL) Data & AI Governance Framework, policies, standards, and processes. The role translates Whole-of-Government (WOG) requirements, including Circular Minutes (CMs), IM8, AI governance directives, and related regulations, into practical institutional processes, controls, and guidance that can be adopted consistently across. The incumbent drives governance maturity, promotes responsible use of data and AI, oversees governance risk assessments, and works closely with Schools and Departments to ensure compliance while enabling innovation and value creation from data and AI. [What you will be working on] 1. Data & AI Governance Strategy, Policy and Standards \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Lead or support the review, enhancement and maintenance of Data & AI Governance Policy, Standards, Frameworks and Guidelines. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Ensure governance policies remain aligned with evolving WOG directives, IM8 requirements, AI governance guidance, PDPA and other regulatory obligations. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Identify policy gaps and recommend improvements to governance frameworks, controls and accountability structures. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Develop governance standards, templates, playbooks, SOPs and guidance materials to support implementation. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Support governance committees and working groups through policy papers, reports and recommendations.\u00a0 2. Policy Interpretation and Translation into Operations \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Interpret government policies, circulars and governance requirements and translate them into practical operational processes. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Lead or support the design of governance workflows covering data access, data sharing, data quality, metadata management, AI assessments, risk approvals and compliance monitoring. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Work with business owners, data owners, system owners and data stewards to embed governance requirements into day-to-day operations. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Develop governance operating procedures that balance compliance with business efficiency. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Establish governance controls, escalation processes and assurance activities.\u00a0 3. Data and AI Risk Management \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Conduct and facilitate Data and AI Governance Risk Assessments for new initiatives, systems, data-sharing requests and AI use cases. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Review AI solutions against governance, ethics, privacy, security and operational risk requirements. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Assess compliance with MOE and WOG governance expectations where applicable. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Recommend risk mitigation measures and monitor implementation. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Maintain governance risk registers and support reporting to management and governance committees. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Support investigation and remediation of governance-related issues and policy breaches.\u00a0 4. Governance Advisory and Compliance Management \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Serve as subject matter expert on Data and AI Governance. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Advise Schools and Departments on governance requirements, interpretation of policies and compliance obligations. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Monitor governance compliance and maturity through reviews, self-assessments and audits. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Develop governance dashboards, metrics and reports for management oversight. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Coordinate responses to governance reviews, audits and assurance exercises. 5. Stakeholder Engagement and Change Management \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Build strong partnerships with Schools, Departments, IT, HR, Legal, Risk and other stakeholders. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Facilitate cross-functional discussions to resolve governance issues and align ownership, accountability and decision-making. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Drive governance awareness programmes, workshops and capability-building initiatives. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Promote a strong culture of responsible, ethical and secure use of data and AI. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Influence stakeholders across all levels through effective communication and engagement. 6. Communication and Governance Enablement \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Simplify complex regulatory and policy requirements into practical guidance understandable by non-specialists. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Prepare awareness materials, presentations, training resources and governance communications. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Communicate governance requirements in clear, business-friendly language. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Drive compliance through education, engagement and stakeholder ownership rather than enforcement alone. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Champion adoption of governance best practices institution-wide. [What we are looking for] \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Qualification in Information Systems, Data Management, Computer Science, Public Policy, Governance, Risk Management, Business, Law or a related discipline. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Relevant certifications in data governance, privacy, risk management, AI governance or cybersecurity will be advantageous. Experience \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0At least 5-8 years of experience in data governance, information governance, risk management, compliance, cybersecurity, AI governance or related fields. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Experience interpreting government regulations, circulars, standards or policy frameworks. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Experience developing policies, governance frameworks, SOPs and operating models. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Experience conducting risk assessments and governance reviews. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Experience working with enterprise stakeholders across multiple business functions. Knowledge & Skills \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Strong understanding of:\u00a0 o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Whole-of-Government Circular Minutes (CMs) o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0IM8 o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Government data governance requirements o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0AI governance and responsible AI principles o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Data protection and privacy requirements o\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Risk management and internal controls \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Excellent written and verbal communication skills. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Ability to explain complex governance concepts in simple, practical terms. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Strong facilitation, negotiation and influencing skills. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Strong stakeholder engagement and collaboration capabilities."}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Tech-for-the-Arts--Media---Design---AL--AI-Hybrid-Cine---Prod-Design-_JR-10000055688": {"title": "School of Tech for the Arts, Media & Design \u2013 AL (AI Hybrid Cine & Prod Design)", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-18\nPart time\n\n[What the role is] The School of Technology for the Arts, Media and Design (STA) provides vocational training in using next-generation technology to enhance and deliver creative expressions in disciplines such as arts and entertainment production management, user experience design, game and gamification design and development, digital content creation and production, graphic design, and audio production. The School is looking to add a dynamic individual to our collaborative team who is experienced in AI Hybrid Production, AI-enhanced Cinematography and Production Design. [What you will be working on] As Associate Lecturer you will: 1.\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Deliver and assess curriculum for youth and adult learners via face-to-face and E-learning modes, in these areas: a.\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0AI Hybrid Production, AI-enhanced Cinematography, Production Design and Workflow b.\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0At least one foundational school discipline area (creativity, story writing and appreciation, photography, working in the creative \u00a0sector, or arts history) 2.\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Supervise programme development activities as assigned such as portfolio development, competition training, and student projects 3.\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Contribute to crafting of curriculum and training materials related to discipline and subject expertise\u00a0 [What we are looking for] \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Relevant qualification and work experience preferably in the field of Media Production and AI Hybrid Production Workflow, applicable to Film Production and Immersive Media. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0A minimum of four years of relevant industry experience preferably in a creative sector. \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0A strong sense of initiative, and the ability to work both independently and as a team-player in collaborative settings \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0The ability to manage projects and events whilst adhering to strict timelines, and conduct post implementation project reviews \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Excellent oral and written communication skills, including the ability to present to large and small groups, and a sensitivity to the needs of people of diverse academic, socio-economic, and cultural backgrounds \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0A self-starter, agile learner, with a personal interest in coaching and mentoring others and managing stakeholder expectations \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Strong analytical, administrative and digitalisation skills including accessing databases and IT-enabled automation Additional Advantages:\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Teaching or professional training experience \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Advance Certificate in Learning and Performance (ACLP) certified\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Management experience \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Experienced in the use of AI Tools with ability in Prompt Engineering, Generative AI processes, and compositing workflow \u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Experienced in the use of software such as Unreal Engine, Adobe Creative Suite, and DaVinci Resolve"}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/Centre-for-Foundational-Studies---Lecturer--Foundational-Studies-_JR-10000050178": {"title": "Centre for Foundational Studies - Lecturer (Foundational Studies)", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-30\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] Centre for Foundational Studies - Lecturer (Foundational Studies) [What you will be working on] \u2022 Facilitate student learning and develop curricula and/or contribute to areas such as: o Social Impact and Community Engagement \u2022 Design and deliver engaging lessons and co-curricular activities to enhance learning and foster holistic student development. \u2022 Create a positive and well-managed classroom environment that drives positive learning outcomes and supports student success. \u2022 Collaborate with module teams to ensure seamless lesson delivery, share best practices, and continuously improve teaching quality. \u2022 Provide pastoral care and academic guidance to support students in their educational and career pathways. \u2022 Contribute to action research projects to enhance teaching and learning competencies and provide valuable insights to the educational community. \u2022 Undertake administrative duties to ensure smooth operations and contribute to the efficiency of the programs at the centre. [What we are looking for] \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Passionate about education, with a keen interest in teaching and mentoring youths.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Self-driven, independent, and proactive, with a strong team-oriented work ethic.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Adaptable to a fast-paced, ever-changing environment.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0People-oriented with strong interpersonal, written, and communication skills.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Proficient in facilitating classroom discussions, mediating diverse opinions, and evaluating reasoning effectively.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Relevant teaching experience, including curriculum development, assessment, and online course design and delivery.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Experience with EdTech tools and AI.\u00a0 \u2022\u00a0\u00a0 \u00a0Hold a qualification in a related field."}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/Office-of-Finance---Deputy-Manager_JR-10000055921": {"title": "Office of Finance - Deputy Manager", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-30\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] Office of Finance - Deputy Manager [What you will be working on] \u2022 Oversee the management of fixed assets, including acquisition, registration, stocktake, transfer, write-off, and disposal, ensuring compliance with organisational policies and audit requirements. \u2022 Administer and monitor projects, including budget tracking, expenditure management, claims processing, funding utilisation, and project reporting. \u2022 Support the annual budgeting process, budget reviews, financial forecasting, and expenditure monitoring to ensure effective utilisation of resources. \u2022 Review and evaluate Approval of Requirements (AOR) submissions to ensure completeness, budget availability, compliance with procurement policies, and alignment with organisational objectives. \u2022 Develop, implement, and review policies, procedures, and internal controls to strengthen governance and operational effectiveness. \u2022 Prepare management reports, financial analyses, presentations, and papers to support decision-making. \u2022 Coordinate and support internal and external audits, ensuring timely resolution of audit findings and recommendations. \u2022 Supervise, mentor, and guide officers within the team to achieve departmental objectives and maintain service excellence. \u2022 Lead or participate in process improvement, digitalisation, and transformation initiatives. \u2022 Perform any other duties and responsibilities as assigned. [What we are looking for] \u2022 Qualification in Accountancy, or its related fields. \u2022 Relevant Public Sector finance experience will be an advantage. \u2022 Proficient in IT tools and productivity software; comfortable adopting AI-assisted tools and digital solutions to improve work efficiency, though expertise is not required. \u2022 Good writing and verbal communication skills. \u2022 A collaborative team player who is meticulous, analytical, systematic, and resourceful."}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Applied-Science---Lecturer-Senior-Lecturer--CET-_JR-10000055923": {"title": "School of Applied Science - Lecturer/Senior Lecturer (CET)", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-30\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] School of Applied Science - Lecturer/Senior Lecturer (Continuing Education & Training) [What you will be working on] \u2022 Design and develop curriculum of Continuing Education & Training (CET) programmes in at least two of the following subject areas: i. AI Applications in Science and Digitalisation ii. Environmental Services and Sustainability iii. Agricultural Sciences iv. Food Manufacturing and Services v. Nutrition, Health and Wellness vi. Data Science and Bioinformatics vii. Biological and Pharmaceutical Sciences viii. Radiation Protection and Safety \u2022 Deliver planned curriculum to adult learners on scheduled weekday evenings or on weekends and participate in assessment activities \u2022 Provide mentorship to adult learners to strengthen their workplace learning \u2022 Contribute to industry engagement related activities and support companies in developing and implementing structured on-the-job training (OJT) plans. \u2022 Lead or participate in applied research and workplace consultancy projects [What we are looking for] \u2022 Relevant qualification in Applied Sciences, Data Science, Artificial Intelligence or other related disciplines. \u2022 At least 5 years of relevant industry experience in Science, Education, Marketing, Workplace Learning, Business Development and/or Consultancy. \u2022 Training and Adult Education (TAE) Workforce Skills Qualification (WSQ) certifications such as Advanced Certificate in Learning and Performance (ACLP), Advanced Certificate in Training and Assessment (ACTA), or Diploma in Adult and Continuing Education (DACE) will be an added advantage. \u2022 Passion for lifelong learning and the ability to facilitate learning for working professionals from diverse backgrounds. \u2022 Strong communication, presentation and interpersonal skills to engage adult learners effectively and foster collaborative relationships with industry partners and stakeholders. \u2022 Effective planning, organisational and classroom facilitation skills, with a focus on practical application and learner-centred teaching. \u2022 Proficient in the use of digital learning technologies, AI tools and online collaboration platforms. \u2022 Prior experience in consultancy and industry projects, and demonstrated ability to apply AI within scientific disciplines and translate industry use cases into practical, hands-on learning experiences will be advantageous."}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Singapore/School-of-Infocomm---Assistant-Director-Capability-and-Industry_JR-10000055944-1": {"title": "School of Infocomm - Assistant Director Capability and Industry", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-30\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] The Assistant Director (Capability and Industry) is a strategic and hands-on technology leader with deep expertise in artificial intelligence, capability development, and business development. This role is responsible for crafting and executing strategies that advance the School's goals in capability building and industry engagement. We are looking for individuals with a proven track record of translating advanced technologies into impactful business solutions, driving organizational capability, and leading cross-functional teams in dynamic and complex environments. [What you will be working on] Spearhead capability development initiatives to strengthen the School\u2019s technology capabilities, focusing on artificial intelligence and emerging technologies. Monitor and anticipate industry trends, evolving \u00a0skillsets, and solution needs to ensure the School remains at the forefront of IT innovation. Align departmental competencies to develop and implement a technology roadmap supporting the School\u2019s long-term strategic goals. Oversee the planning and delivery of technology projects and training programmes in the emerging technology domains. Contribute to the design and delivery of training courses or projects and learner development activities, ensuring learning experiences remain relevant to industry needs and emerging technologies. Lead, coach and develop high-performing teams to drive successful industry projects and impactful training programmes. Forge strategic partnerships with industry leaders, academic institutions, government agencies and other key stakeholders to expand the School's reach and influence. Represent the School at industry events, conferences, and forums to enhance visibility, build partnerships, and stay abreast of the latest industry developments. Drive business growth by identifying new opportunities, developing go-to-market strategies, and closing deals with enterprises and government agencies. Adapt to emerging technologies and changing market landscapes to propose innovative IT solutions. [What we are looking for] Relevant qualification in Computer Science, Information Technology, Engineering or a related field. At least 10 years of professional experience in the IT industry, with a strong technical foundation in artificial intelligence and other emerging technologies. Proven ability to build and nurture high-performing teams. Demonstrated success in capability development, business development, business growth, and technology transformation. Extensive experience in developing and deploying IT solutions involving artificial intelligence and other emerging technologies, including leading the creation and launch of artificial intelligence-powered services. Experience in collaborating with government agencies, research institutes, and industry partners. Excellent communication, stakeholder engagement, and influencing skills, including the ability to engage senior management, external partners, and internal teams."}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/Agriculture-Research-and-Innovation---Research-Scientist--Crop-Health-_JR-10000056163": {"title": "Agriculture Research and Innovation Centre \u2013 Research Scientist (Crop Health)", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-05\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] Agriculture Research and Innovation Centre \u2013 Research Scientist (Crop Health) [What you will be working on] \u2022 Manage the R&D and industry engagement activities of the Crop Health Research Programme in AGRI Centre \u2022 Lead research and consultancy projects relating to crop science and advanced agriculture technologies leading to superior crop health. \u2022 Write project proposals, progress report and make presentation to funding agency for grant funded and consultancy projects. \u2022 Reach out to industry partners and provide consultancy services through research projects. \u2022 Plan, execute and follow-through with the research experiments leading to project deliverables and technology development. \u2022 Conduct literature search, carry out research work and publish articles in internationally reputed Journals/Conferences. \u2022 Provide research support and supervise students and/or technical staff in the team. \u2022 Collaborate with local and international partners for research progress \u2022 Support the operations of school-wide and RP-wide technology events, take on roles to lead in planning and execution of events. \u2022 Assist in outreach activities such as lab visits, technology presentations and training workshops. [What we are looking for] \u2022 The interested candidate must possess Relevant qualification in Plant Science/Life Science/Biotechnology/ or its related field. \u2022 At least 10 years of working experience in the field of plant science or agriculture research with specialization in at least one of the following, plant pathology, Integrated Pest Management, plant physiology, or controlled agriculture, is required. Prior experience with growing and maintaining plants in hydroponics/substrate for urban agriculture or commercial farm will be considered favourable. \u2022 Experience in leading/co-leading research or consultancy projects for industry will advantageous. \u2022 Strong communication and interpersonal skills with the ability to build strong working relationships with people at all levels. \u2022 Possess good multi-tasking skills, with a strong sense of responsibility for completing assigned duties on time. \u2022 Proficient in IT skills. \u2022 Good documentation skills and laboratory techniques. \u2022 Successful candidate will be employed on a contract basis."}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/Office-of-Student-Support---School-Counsellor_JR-10000056755-1": {"title": "Office of Student Support - School Counsellor", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-22\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] The primary role of a School Counsellor is to work with staff, students, parents, external professionals and community agencies to provide quality school counselling support for students\u2019 mental health and social-emotional development. [What you will be working on] Provide individual and group counselling to the student population, with documentation of case notes and records Conduct crisis intervention and management of affected students. Conduct case management with stakeholders (staff, parents and external agencies) to extend support for students Support the counselling team for needs analysis, early identification and referral of students with challenges Plan training programmes and wellness campaigns to raise awareness and understanding of mental health amongst students Conduct workshops for students (mental health issues) and staff (intervention skills) Perform administrative duties such as minute taking, report writing, creating presentation slides, policy drafting, budgeting, procurement, etc. Advise school management on counselling matters Network with relevant external professionals and community agencies Complete ad hoc tasks as assigned by the Office of Student Support [What we are looking for] Relevant qualification in Counselling, with at least two years of work experience in education, counselling and/or volunteer work involving youths Registered counsellor with Singapore Association for Counselling or equivalent; experience with social work or case management will be an advantage Resourceful and able to work independently Strong in administrative and communication skills (spoken and written) Good team player, with strong interpersonal skills IT-savvy and proficient in Microsoft Office applications Applicants with at least 8 years of relevant counselling experience in direct care and support services, preferably within the tertiary education sector, may be considered for a Team Lead position. The School Counsellor (Manager) will provide leadership to the counselling team, coordinate the Polytechnic\u2019s counselling services, and oversee the daily operations of the Student Care Centre."}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Infocomm---Associate-Lecturer--Infocomm-Technology-_JR-10000056547-1": {"title": "School of Infocomm \u2013 Associate Lecturer (Infocomm Technology)", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nPart time\n\n[What the role is] The School of Infocomm is seeking passionate, dynamic industry practitioners and educators to join us as Associate Lecturers. You will contribute to our full-time diploma programmes and/or Continuing Education and Training (CET) adult learning courses across one or more of our key technology domains: Cybersecurity & Digital Forensics, Cloud-Native Infrastructure & DevOps, Artificial Intelligence & Machine Learning, Software & Full-Stack Development, and Financial Technology (FinTech), as well as foundational ICT modules. [What you will be working on] \u2022 Module Delivery & Facilitation: Conduct classes, lab practicals, and workshops in line with polytechnic learning methodologies to achieve designated learning outcomes. \u2022 Assessment & Evaluation: Administer and grade student assessments, practical lab assignments, quizzes, and project deliverables with constructive feedback. \u2022 Curriculum & Instructional Support: Prepare and adapt classroom activities, code demonstrations, and learning resources to reflect real-world industry practices. \u2022 Industry Currency: Bring current industry practices, emerging tools, and ethical perspectives (e.g., data privacy, security governance, AI ethics) into classroom discussions. [What we are looking for] \u2022 Qualifications: Relevent qualification in Computer Science, Information Technology, Cybersecurity, Data Science/AI, Software Engineering, Financial Technology, Computer Engineering, or related disciplines. \u2022 Industry Experience: Minimum 2 years of relevant professional industry experience in your area of technical expertise. \u2022 Passion for Education: A strong commitment to nurturing, mentoring, and engaging youth and adult learners, backed by clear communication and interpersonal skills. Technical Domain Competencies: Applicants should possess hands-on proficiency in at least one (or more) of the following domains: 1. Cybersecurity & Digital Forensics o Penetration Testing / Red Teaming, Vulnerability Assessment o SOC Operations, SIEM, Firewall & Network Security Configuration o Cloud Security, Web Application Security, Secure Coding o Digital Forensics, Incident Response, Malware Analysis o IT Audit, Governance, Risk & Compliance (GRC), Personal Data Protection o Relevant certifications (e.g., CISSP, CISA, CISM, CEH, OSCP) are an advantage. 2. Cloud-Native Infrastructure & DevOps o Scripting and automation using Python, Bash, or PowerShell o CI/CD pipelines, DevOps workflows, and Infrastructure as Code (e.g., Ansible, Terraform) o Containerisation and Orchestration (Docker, Kubernetes) o Public/Private Cloud administration (AWS, Azure, Google Cloud, VMware, OpenStack) o Enterprise networking, server administration (Linux/Windows), and APM/monitoring (Splunk, ELK Stack) o Relevant certifications (e.g., AWS, Azure, RHCSA, CCNA, CKA) are an advantage. 3. Artificial Intelligence & Machine Learning o Machine Learning, Deep Learning, Generative AI, Agentic AI, and NLP/Computer Vision o ML frameworks and libraries (PyTorch, TensorFlow, Keras, Scikit-learn) and Python programming o Data engineering, data preprocessing, feature engineering, and cloud AI deployment pipelines o Foundational mathematics for AI (statistics, probability, linear algebra) and awareness of AI ethics/bias o Relevant cloud AI certifications (Azure AI, AWS Certified Machine Learning, Google Cloud AI) are an advantage. 4. Software & Full-Stack Development o Modern programming languages and frameworks (Python, JavaScript/TypeScript, ES6+, Java/Spring, Node.js, C++) o Front-end and back-end web development, RESTful APIs, and UI/UX design integration o Native or cross-platform mobile application development (e.g., Flutter, React Native) o Software testing (unit, integration, end-to-end), version control (Git), and containerised application deployment via CI/CD 5. Financial Technology (FinTech) o Digital payments, payment gateways, core banking systems, open banking, and embedded finance o RegTech, financial crime technologies, AML/KYC systems, and financial risk compliance o Blockchain technologies, distributed ledgers, smart contract development, and decentralised applications (dApps) o Data analytics, business intelligence, and intelligent process automation in financial workflows"}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Hospitality---Lecturer-Snr-Lecturer--Tourism--Events--Hotel---F-B-_JR-10000056527": {"title": "School of Hospitality - Lecturer/Snr Lecturer (Tourism, Events, Hotel & F&B)", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nFull time\n\n[What the role is] We are seeking a dynamic and passionate individual to join RP as a Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in the School of Hospitality. In this dual-function role, you will inspire the next generation of professionals through academic teaching and spearhead the strategic planning, execution, and management of our student internship programme. You will be the pivotal bridge between the institution and industry, managing high-quality local and overseas internship placements to ensure our students gain robust, real-world industry experience and global perspectives. [What you will be working on] Job Responsibilities: \u2022 Foster a nurturing environment for students through comprehensive pastoral care and offer guidance and support in their educational and career journeys. \u2022 Develop and review module curriculum with engaging learning activities that align with the prescribed programme and module outcomes for both pre-employment training (PET) and continuing education and training (CET). \u2022 Deliver lessons effectively through good class management and with efficacious outcomes. \u2022 Supervise students in projects and other curricular activities. \u2022 Set, invigilate, and grade assessments. \u2022 Undertake administrative duties and academic affairs related to a programme. \u2022 Oversee the end-to-end administration of the student internship programme for the school. \u2022 Establish clear assessment rubrics, compliance guidelines, and evaluation frameworks for both local and overseas internships. \u2022 Conduct internship briefings, pre-departure orientations (for overseas stints), and post-internship debriefs for students. \u2022 Manage student safety, welfare, and crisis protocols, particularly for students stationed abroad. [What we are looking for] \u2022 Possess excellent interpersonal, communication, management, and writing skills. \u2022 Demonstrate resourcefulness as a team player while exhibiting trustworthiness, independence, and a proactive work ethic. \u2022 Strong conceptual thinking skills with an ability to problem solve and recommend solutions. \u2022 Able to facilitate classroom discussions, adeptly mediate different opinions and evaluate reasoning. \u2022 Able to introduce effective interventions by analysing students' results and performance. \u2022 Digital literacy (using information ethically and effectively), and the ability to collaborate and communicate using digital tools. \u2022 AI literacy that includes AI fundamentals, data science, AI tools and automation, Natural Language Processing (NLP), AI ethics, and prompt engineering. \u2022 Teaching experience in any of the following domains is preferred: > Hospitality and Tourism Management > Events and Project Management > Hotel and Leisure Management > Restaurant and Culinary Management"}}, "rows": {"https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Hospitality---Lecturer-Senior-Lecturer--Continuing-Educatn---Training-_JR-10000044130": {"school_id": 1865, "posting_url": "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/School-of-Hospitality---Lecturer-Senior-Lecturer--Continuing-Educatn---Training-_JR-10000044130", "job_title_in_post": "School of Hospitality - Lecturer/Snr Lecturer (Continuing Education & Training)", "position_type": "Lecturer", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "School of Hospitality", "area_key_words": "Hospitality", "deadline_of_application": "", "posted_date": "2026-09-02", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/PublicServiceCareers/job/Republic-Polytechnic/Office-of-Finance---Executive--2-year-contract-_JR-10000051618": {"school_id": 1865, "posting_url": "https://sggovterp.wd102.myworkdayjobs.com/Pu